// Generated from compiled and tested Java sources; code and output are copied verbatim from real runs.
window.SOLUTIONS = window.SOLUTIONS || [];
window.SOLUTIONS.push({"id":"library-management-system","intro":"The system is built one requirement at a time, in the same order as the requirements list. Titles and physical copies are separate types from the start, because almost every later rule (limits, reservations, fines) depends on that split. Concurrency is handled where the data lives: a copy claims itself atomically, and the lending service always locks the member first and the book second. Every file below compiles together with plain `javac`, and the output and test results shown are from a real run.","steps":[{"title":"Requirement 1: titles versus copies, and search","text":"Model what is true of every copy once, in `Book`, and what is true of one object on a shelf in `BookCopy`. A copy can claim itself with `tryCheckOut`, which is `synchronized` and returns false if someone else already has it. That single method is what guarantees a copy is never lent twice. `Catalog` answers the search requirement: an exact ISBN, or a case-insensitive fragment of the title or an author, sorted by title so results are stable.","code":[{"file":"Book.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class Book {\n  private final String isbn;\n  private final String title;\n  private final List<String> authors;\n  private final List<BookCopy> copies = new ArrayList<>();\n\n  public Book(String isbn, String title, List<String> authors) {\n    this.isbn = isbn;\n    this.title = title;\n    this.authors = authors;\n  }\n\n  public BookCopy addCopy(String barcode) {\n    BookCopy c = new BookCopy(barcode, this);\n    copies.add(c);\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  public List<BookCopy> findAllCopies() { return copies; }\n\n  public long availableCount() {\n    return copies.stream().filter(BookCopy::isAvailable).count();\n  }\n\n  public String getIsbn() { return isbn; }\n  public String getTitle() { return title; }\n  public List<String> getAuthors() { return authors; }\n}"},{"file":"BookCopy.java","body":"public class BookCopy {\n  private final String barcode;\n  private final Book book;\n  private boolean onLoan;\n\n  BookCopy(String barcode, Book book) {\n    this.barcode = barcode;\n    this.book = book;\n  }\n\n  // Atomically claim the copy; false if someone else already has it.\n  synchronized boolean tryCheckOut() {\n    if (onLoan) return false;\n    onLoan = true;\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  synchronized void markReturned() { onLoan = false; }\n  public synchronized boolean isAvailable() { return !onLoan; }\n\n  public Book getBook() { return book; }\n  public String getBarcode() { return barcode; }\n}"},{"file":"Catalog.java","body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.Collectors;\n\npublic class Catalog {\n  private final Map<String, Book> byIsbn = new HashMap<>();\n\n  public void add(Book b) { byIsbn.put(b.getIsbn(), b); }\n\n  public Optional<Book> byIsbn(String isbn) { return Optional.ofNullable(byIsbn.get(isbn)); }\n\n  // Matches an exact ISBN, or a case-insensitive fragment of the title or an author.\n  public List<Book> search(String query) {\n    String q = query.toLowerCase();\n    return byIsbn.values().stream()\n        .filter(b -> b.getIsbn().equals(query)\n            || b.getTitle().toLowerCase().contains(q)\n            || b.getAuthors().stream().anyMatch(a -> a.toLowerCase().contains(q)))\n        .sorted(Comparator.comparing(Book::getTitle))\n        .collect(Collectors.toList());\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirements 2 and 3: check out, the five-book limit and the 14-day due date","text":"A `Loan` stores the dates, so the due date and any fine can be derived later with no extra state. `Member` counts only active loans. `checkOut` does four things in order: enforce the limit, make sure a copy exists, make sure the remaining copies are not earmarked for someone on the waiting list (the `canBorrow` line, explained in step 5), then claim a copy atomically. The whole method runs inside `synchronized (member)` then `synchronized (book)`. Always taking the locks in that order is what makes deadlock impossible, and the member lock is what stops one person from sneaking past the limit with several simultaneous requests.","code":[{"file":"Loan.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\n\npublic class Loan {\n  private final BookCopy copy;\n  private final Member member;\n  private final LocalDate checkedOutOn;\n  private final LocalDate dueOn;\n  private LocalDate returnedOn;\n\n  public Loan(BookCopy copy, Member member, LocalDate checkedOutOn, int loanDays) {\n    this.copy = copy;\n    this.member = member;\n    this.checkedOutOn = checkedOutOn;\n    this.dueOn = checkedOutOn.plusDays(loanDays);\n  }\n\n  void close(LocalDate on) { this.returnedOn = on; }\n\n  public boolean isActive() { return returnedOn == null; }\n  public BookCopy getCopy() { return copy; }\n  public Member getMember() { return member; }\n  public LocalDate getCheckedOutOn() { return checkedOutOn; }\n  public LocalDate getDueOn() { return dueOn; }\n  public LocalDate getReturnedOn() { return returnedOn; }\n}"},{"file":"Member.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class Member {\n  public static final int MAX_LOANS = 5;\n\n  private final String id;\n  private final String name;\n  private final MemberType type;\n  private final List<Loan> loans = new ArrayList<>();\n\n  public Member(String id, String name) { this(id, name, MemberType.STANDARD); }\n\n  public Member(String id, String name, MemberType type) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.name = name;\n    this.type = type;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized long activeLoanCount() {\n    return loans.stream().filter(Loan::isActive).count();\n  }\n\n  synchronized void addLoan(Loan l) { loans.add(l); }\n\n  public String getId() { return id; }\n  public String getName() { return name; }\n  public MemberType getType() { return type; }\n}"},{"file":"LendingService.java  ›  checkOut","body":"// Lock order is always member, then book, so two threads can never deadlock.\npublic Loan checkOut(Member member, Book book) {\n  synchronized (member) {\n    synchronized (book) {\n      if (member.activeLoanCount() >= Member.MAX_LOANS)\n        throw new LoanLimitException(member.getId());\n      if (book.availableCount() == 0)\n        throw new NoCopyAvailableException(\"No copy of '\" + book.getTitle() + \"' is available\");\n      if (!reservations.canBorrow(member, book))\n        throw new NoCopyAvailableException(\"Remaining copies of '\" + book.getTitle() + \"' are reserved for other members\");\n\n      for (BookCopy copy : book.findAllCopies()) {\n        if (copy.tryCheckOut()) {                 // atomic claim of the physical copy\n          Loan loan = new Loan(copy, member, LocalDate.now(clock), LOAN_DAYS);\n          member.addLoan(loan);\n          reservations.fulfil(member, book);\n          return loan;\n        }\n      }\n      throw new NoCopyAvailableException(\"No copy of '\" + book.getTitle() + \"' is available\");   // lost a race for the copy\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"LoanLimitException.java","body":"public class LoanLimitException extends RuntimeException {\n  public LoanLimitException(String memberId) {\n    super(\"Member \" + memberId + \" already has \" + Member.MAX_LOANS + \" books on loan\");\n  }\n}"},{"file":"NoCopyAvailableException.java","body":"public class NoCopyAvailableException extends RuntimeException {\n  public NoCopyAvailableException(String message) { super(message); }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 4: fines that can change","text":"Return closes the loan, frees the copy and asks a `FineCalculator` what is owed. The calculator is an interface because the product team will ask for caps and member discounts. Each rule is a small class that can wrap another one: a per-day fine, a cap on top of it, and a premium discount on top of that. The three are composed in `Main` without touching `LendingService`.","code":[{"file":"FineCalculator.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\n\npublic interface FineCalculator {\n  Money fineFor(Loan loan, LocalDate returnedOn);\n}"},{"file":"PerDayFine.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;\n\npublic class PerDayFine implements FineCalculator {\n  private final Money perDay;\n\n  public PerDayFine(Money perDay) { this.perDay = perDay; }\n\n  public Money fineFor(Loan loan, LocalDate returnedOn) {\n    long late = ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(loan.getDueOn(), returnedOn);\n    return late <= 0 ? Money.ZERO : perDay.times(late);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"CappedFine.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\n\npublic class CappedFine implements FineCalculator {\n  private final FineCalculator inner;\n  private final Money cap;\n\n  public CappedFine(FineCalculator inner, Money cap) {\n    this.inner = inner;\n    this.cap = cap;\n  }\n\n  public Money fineFor(Loan loan, LocalDate returnedOn) {\n    Money fine = inner.fineFor(loan, returnedOn);\n    return fine.isGreaterThan(cap) ? cap : fine;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"MemberTypeFine.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\n\n// Premium members get a percentage off whatever the wrapped rule produces.\npublic class MemberTypeFine implements FineCalculator {\n  private final FineCalculator inner;\n  private final int premiumDiscountPercent;\n\n  public MemberTypeFine(FineCalculator inner, int premiumDiscountPercent) {\n    this.inner = inner;\n    this.premiumDiscountPercent = premiumDiscountPercent;\n  }\n\n  public Money fineFor(Loan loan, LocalDate returnedOn) {\n    Money fine = inner.fineFor(loan, returnedOn);\n    if (loan.getMember().getType() != MemberType.PREMIUM) return fine;\n    return fine.percent(100 - premiumDiscountPercent);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"LendingService.java  ›  returnCopy","body":"public Money returnCopy(Loan loan) {\n  Book book = loan.getCopy().getBook();\n  Money fine;\n  Member promoted;\n  synchronized (book) {\n    if (!loan.isActive()) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Loan already returned\");\n    LocalDate today = LocalDate.now(clock);\n    loan.close(today);\n    loan.getCopy().markReturned();\n    fine = fines.fineFor(loan, today);\n    promoted = reservations.promoteNext(book).orElse(null);\n  }\n  if (promoted != null) reservations.notifyAvailable(promoted, book);   // outside the lock\n  return fine;\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 5: reservations and notifications","text":"A title with no free copy gets a first-in-first-out queue. When a copy comes back, `promoteNext` moves the first waiter into a `ready` set, which earmarks one copy for them: `canBorrow` lets a member through only if they are `ready` or if there are more free copies than earmarked ones. That is how \"a reserved title must go to the right member\" is enforced rather than just announced. The notification itself happens after the lock is released, through `ReservationListener`s, so email, SMS or push are added by registering another listener and nothing in the lending flow changes.","code":[{"file":"ReservationService.java","body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\n// waiting: members queued for a title. ready: members told a copy is theirs to borrow.\n// Each \"ready\" member earmarks one available copy, so nobody else can take it.\npublic class ReservationService {\n  private final Map<String, Deque<Member>> waiting = new HashMap<>();\n  private final Map<String, Set<Member>> ready = new HashMap<>();\n  private final List<ReservationListener> listeners = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public void addListener(ReservationListener l) { listeners.add(l); }\n\n  public synchronized void reserve(Member member, Book book) {\n    String isbn = book.getIsbn();\n    if (book.availableCount() > readyCount(isbn))\n      throw new IllegalStateException(\"A copy of '\" + book.getTitle() + \"' is available; borrow it instead\");\n    Deque<Member> q = waiting.computeIfAbsent(isbn, k -> new ArrayDeque<>());\n    if (q.contains(member) || ready.getOrDefault(isbn, Set.of()).contains(member))\n      throw new IllegalStateException(member.getId() + \" already reserved '\" + book.getTitle() + \"'\");\n    q.addLast(member);\n  }\n\n  // Called inside the book's lock: earmark the returned copy for the first waiter.\n  synchronized Optional<Member> promoteNext(Book book) {\n    Deque<Member> q = waiting.get(book.getIsbn());\n    if (q == null || q.isEmpty()) return Optional.empty();\n    Member next = q.pollFirst();\n    ready.computeIfAbsent(book.getIsbn(), k -> new LinkedHashSet<>()).add(next);\n    return Optional.of(next);\n  }\n\n  // Called outside any lock: listeners may be slow (email, SMS).\n  void notifyAvailable(Member member, Book book) {\n    listeners.forEach(l -> l.onBookAvailable(member, book));\n  }\n\n  synchronized boolean canBorrow(Member member, Book book) {\n    String isbn = book.getIsbn();\n    return ready.getOrDefault(isbn, Set.of()).contains(member)\n        || book.availableCount() > readyCount(isbn);\n  }\n\n  synchronized void fulfil(Member member, Book book) {\n    Set<Member> r = ready.get(book.getIsbn());\n    if (r != null) r.remove(member);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized int waitingCount(Book book) {\n    return waiting.getOrDefault(book.getIsbn(), new ArrayDeque<>()).size();\n  }\n\n  private int readyCount(String isbn) { return ready.getOrDefault(isbn, Set.of()).size(); }\n}"},{"file":"ReservationListener.java","body":"public interface ReservationListener {\n  void onBookAvailable(Member member, Book book);\n}"},{"file":"MessageChannel.java","body":"@FunctionalInterface\npublic interface MessageChannel {\n  void send(String memberId, String text);\n}"},{"file":"EmailReservationListener.java","body":"public class EmailReservationListener implements ReservationListener {\n  private final MessageChannel email;\n\n  public EmailReservationListener(MessageChannel email) { this.email = email; }\n\n  public void onBookAvailable(Member member, Book book) {\n    email.send(member.getId(), \"'\" + book.getTitle() + \"' is now available for you.\");\n  }\n}"},{"file":"SmsReservationListener.java","body":"public class SmsReservationListener implements ReservationListener {\n  private final MessageChannel sms;\n\n  public SmsReservationListener(MessageChannel sms) { this.sms = sms; }\n\n  public void onBookAvailable(Member member, Book book) {\n    sms.send(member.getId(), \"Your reserved book is ready: \" + book.getTitle());\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"Wiring it together","text":"The clock is injected, so tests and the demo can move time forward instead of waiting two weeks. The fine rule is built by stacking three small objects.","code":[{"file":"Main.java  ›  wiring","body":"MutableClock clock = new MutableClock(Instant.parse(\"2026-01-05T09:00:00Z\"));\nReservationService reservations = new ReservationService();\nreservations.addListener(new EmailReservationListener(new ConsoleChannel(\"EMAIL\")));\nreservations.addListener(new SmsReservationListener(new ConsoleChannel(\"SMS\")));\n\n// Per-day fine of $0.50, capped at $10, premium members pay half.\nFineCalculator fines = new MemberTypeFine(new CappedFine(new PerDayFine(Money.ofCents(50)), Money.dollars(10)), 50);\nLendingService lending = new LendingService(clock, fines, reservations);\n\nCatalog catalog = new Catalog();\nBook cleanCode = book(catalog, \"9780132350884\", \"Clean Code\", \"Robert C. Martin\", 2);"}]}],"files":[{"file":"Money.java","body":"public final class Money {\n  public static final Money ZERO = new Money(0);\n\n  private final long cents;\n\n  private Money(long cents) { this.cents = cents; }\n\n  public static Money ofCents(long cents) { return new Money(cents); }\n  public static Money dollars(long dollars) { return new Money(dollars * 100); }\n\n  public Money plus(Money other) { return new Money(cents + other.cents); }\n  public Money times(long n) { return new Money(cents * n); }\n  public Money percent(int p) { return new Money(cents * p / 100); }\n  public boolean isGreaterThan(Money other) { return cents > other.cents; }\n  public long cents() { return cents; }\n\n  @Override public boolean equals(Object o) { return o instanceof Money m && m.cents == cents; }\n  @Override public int hashCode() { return Long.hashCode(cents); }\n  @Override public String toString() { return String.format(\"$%d.%02d\", cents / 100, cents % 100); }\n}"},{"file":"MutableClock.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.time.ZoneId;\nimport java.time.ZoneOffset;\n\n// A clock we can move forward, so overdue loans can be shown and tested without waiting.\npublic class MutableClock extends Clock {\n  private Instant now;\n\n  public MutableClock(Instant start) { this.now = start; }\n\n  public synchronized void advance(Duration d) { now = now.plus(d); }\n\n  @Override public ZoneId getZone() { return ZoneOffset.UTC; }\n  @Override public Clock withZone(ZoneId zone) { return this; }\n  @Override public synchronized Instant instant() { return now; }\n}"},{"file":"Book.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class Book {\n  private final String isbn;\n  private final String title;\n  private final List<String> authors;\n  private final List<BookCopy> copies = new ArrayList<>();\n\n  public Book(String isbn, String title, List<String> authors) {\n    this.isbn = isbn;\n    this.title = title;\n    this.authors = authors;\n  }\n\n  public BookCopy addCopy(String barcode) {\n    BookCopy c = new BookCopy(barcode, this);\n    copies.add(c);\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  public List<BookCopy> findAllCopies() { return copies; }\n\n  public long availableCount() {\n    return copies.stream().filter(BookCopy::isAvailable).count();\n  }\n\n  public String getIsbn() { return isbn; }\n  public String getTitle() { return title; }\n  public List<String> getAuthors() { return authors; }\n}"},{"file":"BookCopy.java","body":"public class BookCopy {\n  private final String barcode;\n  private final Book book;\n  private boolean onLoan;\n\n  BookCopy(String barcode, Book book) {\n    this.barcode = barcode;\n    this.book = book;\n  }\n\n  // Atomically claim the copy; false if someone else already has it.\n  synchronized boolean tryCheckOut() {\n    if (onLoan) return false;\n    onLoan = true;\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  synchronized void markReturned() { onLoan = false; }\n  public synchronized boolean isAvailable() { return !onLoan; }\n\n  public Book getBook() { return book; }\n  public String getBarcode() { return barcode; }\n}"},{"file":"Catalog.java","body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.Collectors;\n\npublic class Catalog {\n  private final Map<String, Book> byIsbn = new HashMap<>();\n\n  public void add(Book b) { byIsbn.put(b.getIsbn(), b); }\n\n  public Optional<Book> byIsbn(String isbn) { return Optional.ofNullable(byIsbn.get(isbn)); }\n\n  // Matches an exact ISBN, or a case-insensitive fragment of the title or an author.\n  public List<Book> search(String query) {\n    String q = query.toLowerCase();\n    return byIsbn.values().stream()\n        .filter(b -> b.getIsbn().equals(query)\n            || b.getTitle().toLowerCase().contains(q)\n            || b.getAuthors().stream().anyMatch(a -> a.toLowerCase().contains(q)))\n        .sorted(Comparator.comparing(Book::getTitle))\n        .collect(Collectors.toList());\n  }\n}"},{"file":"MemberType.java","body":"public enum MemberType { STANDARD, PREMIUM }"},{"file":"Member.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class Member {\n  public static final int MAX_LOANS = 5;\n\n  private final String id;\n  private final String name;\n  private final MemberType type;\n  private final List<Loan> loans = new ArrayList<>();\n\n  public Member(String id, String name) { this(id, name, MemberType.STANDARD); }\n\n  public Member(String id, String name, MemberType type) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.name = name;\n    this.type = type;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized long activeLoanCount() {\n    return loans.stream().filter(Loan::isActive).count();\n  }\n\n  synchronized void addLoan(Loan l) { loans.add(l); }\n\n  public String getId() { return id; }\n  public String getName() { return name; }\n  public MemberType getType() { return type; }\n}"},{"file":"Loan.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\n\npublic class Loan {\n  private final BookCopy copy;\n  private final Member member;\n  private final LocalDate checkedOutOn;\n  private final LocalDate dueOn;\n  private LocalDate returnedOn;\n\n  public Loan(BookCopy copy, Member member, LocalDate checkedOutOn, int loanDays) {\n    this.copy = copy;\n    this.member = member;\n    this.checkedOutOn = checkedOutOn;\n    this.dueOn = checkedOutOn.plusDays(loanDays);\n  }\n\n  void close(LocalDate on) { this.returnedOn = on; }\n\n  public boolean isActive() { return returnedOn == null; }\n  public BookCopy getCopy() { return copy; }\n  public Member getMember() { return member; }\n  public LocalDate getCheckedOutOn() { return checkedOutOn; }\n  public LocalDate getDueOn() { return dueOn; }\n  public LocalDate getReturnedOn() { return returnedOn; }\n}"},{"file":"LoanLimitException.java","body":"public class LoanLimitException extends RuntimeException {\n  public LoanLimitException(String memberId) {\n    super(\"Member \" + memberId + \" already has \" + Member.MAX_LOANS + \" books on loan\");\n  }\n}"},{"file":"NoCopyAvailableException.java","body":"public class NoCopyAvailableException extends RuntimeException {\n  public NoCopyAvailableException(String message) { super(message); }\n}"},{"file":"FineCalculator.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\n\npublic interface FineCalculator {\n  Money fineFor(Loan loan, LocalDate returnedOn);\n}"},{"file":"PerDayFine.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;\n\npublic class PerDayFine implements FineCalculator {\n  private final Money perDay;\n\n  public PerDayFine(Money perDay) { this.perDay = perDay; }\n\n  public Money fineFor(Loan loan, LocalDate returnedOn) {\n    long late = ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(loan.getDueOn(), returnedOn);\n    return late <= 0 ? Money.ZERO : perDay.times(late);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"CappedFine.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\n\npublic class CappedFine implements FineCalculator {\n  private final FineCalculator inner;\n  private final Money cap;\n\n  public CappedFine(FineCalculator inner, Money cap) {\n    this.inner = inner;\n    this.cap = cap;\n  }\n\n  public Money fineFor(Loan loan, LocalDate returnedOn) {\n    Money fine = inner.fineFor(loan, returnedOn);\n    return fine.isGreaterThan(cap) ? cap : fine;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"MemberTypeFine.java","body":"import java.time.LocalDate;\n\n// Premium members get a percentage off whatever the wrapped rule produces.\npublic class MemberTypeFine implements FineCalculator {\n  private final FineCalculator inner;\n  private final int premiumDiscountPercent;\n\n  public MemberTypeFine(FineCalculator inner, int premiumDiscountPercent) {\n    this.inner = inner;\n    this.premiumDiscountPercent = premiumDiscountPercent;\n  }\n\n  public Money fineFor(Loan loan, LocalDate returnedOn) {\n    Money fine = inner.fineFor(loan, returnedOn);\n    if (loan.getMember().getType() != MemberType.PREMIUM) return fine;\n    return fine.percent(100 - premiumDiscountPercent);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"MessageChannel.java","body":"@FunctionalInterface\npublic interface MessageChannel {\n  void send(String memberId, String text);\n}"},{"file":"ConsoleChannel.java","body":"public class ConsoleChannel implements MessageChannel {\n  private final String label;\n\n  public ConsoleChannel(String label) { this.label = label; }\n\n  public void send(String memberId, String text) {\n    System.out.println(\"  [\" + label + \"] to \" + memberId + \": \" + text);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"ReservationListener.java","body":"public interface ReservationListener {\n  void onBookAvailable(Member member, Book book);\n}"},{"file":"EmailReservationListener.java","body":"public class EmailReservationListener implements ReservationListener {\n  private final MessageChannel email;\n\n  public EmailReservationListener(MessageChannel email) { this.email = email; }\n\n  public void onBookAvailable(Member member, Book book) {\n    email.send(member.getId(), \"'\" + book.getTitle() + \"' is now available for you.\");\n  }\n}"},{"file":"SmsReservationListener.java","body":"public class SmsReservationListener implements ReservationListener {\n  private final MessageChannel sms;\n\n  public SmsReservationListener(MessageChannel sms) { this.sms = sms; }\n\n  public void onBookAvailable(Member member, Book book) {\n    sms.send(member.getId(), \"Your reserved book is ready: \" + book.getTitle());\n  }\n}"},{"file":"ReservationService.java","body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\n// waiting: members queued for a title. ready: members told a copy is theirs to borrow.\n// Each \"ready\" member earmarks one available copy, so nobody else can take it.\npublic class ReservationService {\n  private final Map<String, Deque<Member>> waiting = new HashMap<>();\n  private final Map<String, Set<Member>> ready = new HashMap<>();\n  private final List<ReservationListener> listeners = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public void addListener(ReservationListener l) { listeners.add(l); }\n\n  public synchronized void reserve(Member member, Book book) {\n    String isbn = book.getIsbn();\n    if (book.availableCount() > readyCount(isbn))\n      throw new IllegalStateException(\"A copy of '\" + book.getTitle() + \"' is available; borrow it instead\");\n    Deque<Member> q = waiting.computeIfAbsent(isbn, k -> new ArrayDeque<>());\n    if (q.contains(member) || ready.getOrDefault(isbn, Set.of()).contains(member))\n      throw new IllegalStateException(member.getId() + \" already reserved '\" + book.getTitle() + \"'\");\n    q.addLast(member);\n  }\n\n  // Called inside the book's lock: earmark the returned copy for the first waiter.\n  synchronized Optional<Member> promoteNext(Book book) {\n    Deque<Member> q = waiting.get(book.getIsbn());\n    if (q == null || q.isEmpty()) return Optional.empty();\n    Member next = q.pollFirst();\n    ready.computeIfAbsent(book.getIsbn(), k -> new LinkedHashSet<>()).add(next);\n    return Optional.of(next);\n  }\n\n  // Called outside any lock: listeners may be slow (email, SMS).\n  void notifyAvailable(Member member, Book book) {\n    listeners.forEach(l -> l.onBookAvailable(member, book));\n  }\n\n  synchronized boolean canBorrow(Member member, Book book) {\n    String isbn = book.getIsbn();\n    return ready.getOrDefault(isbn, Set.of()).contains(member)\n        || book.availableCount() > readyCount(isbn);\n  }\n\n  synchronized void fulfil(Member member, Book book) {\n    Set<Member> r = ready.get(book.getIsbn());\n    if (r != null) r.remove(member);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized int waitingCount(Book book) {\n    return waiting.getOrDefault(book.getIsbn(), new ArrayDeque<>()).size();\n  }\n\n  private int readyCount(String isbn) { return ready.getOrDefault(isbn, Set.of()).size(); }\n}"},{"file":"LendingService.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\n\npublic class LendingService {\n  private static final int LOAN_DAYS = 14;\n\n  private final Clock clock;\n  private final FineCalculator fines;\n  private final ReservationService reservations;\n\n  public LendingService(Clock clock, FineCalculator fines, ReservationService reservations) {\n    this.clock = clock;\n    this.fines = fines;\n    this.reservations = reservations;\n  }\n\n  // Lock order is always member, then book, so two threads can never deadlock.\n  public Loan checkOut(Member member, Book book) {\n    synchronized (member) {\n      synchronized (book) {\n        if (member.activeLoanCount() >= Member.MAX_LOANS)\n          throw new LoanLimitException(member.getId());\n        if (book.availableCount() == 0)\n          throw new NoCopyAvailableException(\"No copy of '\" + book.getTitle() + \"' is available\");\n        if (!reservations.canBorrow(member, book))\n          throw new NoCopyAvailableException(\"Remaining copies of '\" + book.getTitle() + \"' are reserved for other members\");\n\n        for (BookCopy copy : book.findAllCopies()) {\n          if (copy.tryCheckOut()) {                 // atomic claim of the physical copy\n            Loan loan = new Loan(copy, member, LocalDate.now(clock), LOAN_DAYS);\n            member.addLoan(loan);\n            reservations.fulfil(member, book);\n            return loan;\n          }\n        }\n        throw new NoCopyAvailableException(\"No copy of '\" + book.getTitle() + \"' is available\");   // lost a race for the copy\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  public Money returnCopy(Loan loan) {\n    Book book = loan.getCopy().getBook();\n    Money fine;\n    Member promoted;\n    synchronized (book) {\n      if (!loan.isActive()) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Loan already returned\");\n      LocalDate today = LocalDate.now(clock);\n      loan.close(today);\n      loan.getCopy().markReturned();\n      fine = fines.fineFor(loan, today);\n      promoted = reservations.promoteNext(book).orElse(null);\n    }\n    if (promoted != null) reservations.notifyAvailable(promoted, book);   // outside the lock\n    return fine;\n  }\n}"}],"driver":{"text":"The demo walks every requirement: search, due dates, the limit, a two-member race for the last copy, late fines with a cap and a premium discount, and a reservation queue with email and SMS.","file":"Main.java","body":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\npublic class Main {\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    MutableClock clock = new MutableClock(Instant.parse(\"2026-01-05T09:00:00Z\"));\n    ReservationService reservations = new ReservationService();\n    reservations.addListener(new EmailReservationListener(new ConsoleChannel(\"EMAIL\")));\n    reservations.addListener(new SmsReservationListener(new ConsoleChannel(\"SMS\")));\n\n    // Per-day fine of $0.50, capped at $10, premium members pay half.\n    FineCalculator fines = new MemberTypeFine(new CappedFine(new PerDayFine(Money.ofCents(50)), Money.dollars(10)), 50);\n    LendingService lending = new LendingService(clock, fines, reservations);\n\n    Catalog catalog = new Catalog();\n    Book cleanCode = book(catalog, \"9780132350884\", \"Clean Code\", \"Robert C. Martin\", 2);\n    Book refactoring = book(catalog, \"9780134757599\", \"Refactoring\", \"Martin Fowler\", 1);\n    Book patterns = book(catalog, \"9780201633610\", \"Design Patterns\", \"Erich Gamma\", 1);\n    Book dune = book(catalog, \"9780441172719\", \"Dune\", \"Frank Herbert\", 1);\n    Book[] novels = new Book[6];\n    for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) novels[i] = book(catalog, \"978000000000\" + i, \"Novel \" + (i + 1), \"A. Writer\", 1);\n\n    Member alice = new Member(\"alice\", \"Alice\");\n    Member bob = new Member(\"bob\", \"Bob\");\n    Member carol = new Member(\"carol\", \"Carol\");\n    Member priya = new Member(\"priya\", \"Priya\", MemberType.PREMIUM);\n\n    System.out.println(\"== 1. Search ==\");\n    show(\"'martin'\", catalog.search(\"martin\"));\n    show(\"ISBN 9780441172719\", catalog.search(\"9780441172719\"));\n    show(\"'CLEAN'\", catalog.search(\"CLEAN\"));\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 2. Check out with a 14-day due date ==\");\n    Loan first = lending.checkOut(alice, cleanCode);\n    System.out.println(\"Alice borrowed Clean Code on \" + first.getCheckedOutOn() + \", due \" + first.getDueOn());\n    Loan second = lending.checkOut(bob, cleanCode);\n    System.out.println(\"Bob borrowed the second copy; Clean Code available copies = \" + cleanCode.availableCount());\n    try {\n      lending.checkOut(carol, cleanCode);\n    } catch (NoCopyAvailableException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Carol refused: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 3. Five-book limit ==\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) lending.checkOut(carol, novels[i]);\n    System.out.println(\"Carol now holds \" + carol.activeLoanCount() + \" books\");\n    try {\n      lending.checkOut(carol, novels[5]);\n    } catch (LoanLimitException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Refused: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 4. Two members race for the last copy ==\");\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);\n    CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    AtomicInteger won = new AtomicInteger(), lost = new AtomicInteger();\n    for (Member m : List.of(alice, priya)) {\n      pool.submit(() -> {\n        try {\n          go.await();\n          lending.checkOut(m, patterns);\n          won.incrementAndGet();\n        } catch (NoCopyAvailableException e) {\n          lost.incrementAndGet();\n        } catch (InterruptedException ignored) { }\n      });\n    }\n    go.countDown();\n    pool.shutdown();\n    pool.awaitTermination(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n    System.out.println(\"Design Patterns: winners=\" + won + \", losers=\" + lost + \", available=\" + patterns.availableCount());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 5. Fines on late returns ==\");\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofDays(20));                       // day 20; due on day 14\n    Money f1 = lending.returnCopy(first);\n    System.out.println(\"Alice returns Clean Code 6 days late: fine \" + f1);\n    Loan bobsLoan = second;\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofDays(30));                       // 36 days late in total\n    Money f2 = lending.returnCopy(bobsLoan);\n    System.out.println(\"Bob returns 36 days late: fine \" + f2 + \" (capped at $10.00)\");\n    Loan priyaLoan = lending.checkOut(priya, refactoring);\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofDays(34));                       // 20 days late\n    Money f3 = lending.returnCopy(priyaLoan);\n    System.out.println(\"Priya (premium) returns 20 days late: fine \" + f3 + \" (half of $10.00 cap)\");\n    Loan onTime = lending.checkOut(bob, refactoring);\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofDays(3));\n    System.out.println(\"Bob returns on time: fine \" + lending.returnCopy(onTime));\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 6. Reservations ==\");\n    Loan duneLoan = lending.checkOut(alice, dune);\n    try {\n      reservations.reserve(priya, refactoring);\n    } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Cannot reserve: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n    reservations.reserve(bob, dune);\n    reservations.reserve(priya, dune);\n    System.out.println(\"Waiting for Dune: \" + reservations.waitingCount(dune));\n    System.out.println(\"Alice returns Dune:\");\n    lending.returnCopy(duneLoan);\n    try {\n      lending.checkOut(alice, dune);\n    } catch (NoCopyAvailableException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Alice tries to borrow it again: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n    Loan bobDune = lending.checkOut(bob, dune);\n    System.out.println(\"Bob, first in the queue, borrows Dune\");\n    System.out.println(\"Bob returns Dune:\");\n    lending.returnCopy(bobDune);\n  }\n\n  private static Book book(Catalog catalog, String isbn, String title, String author, int copies) {\n    Book b = new Book(isbn, title, List.of(author));\n    for (int i = 1; i <= copies; i++) b.addCopy(isbn + \"-\" + i);\n    catalog.add(b);\n    return b;\n  }\n\n  private static void show(String label, List<Book> results) {\n    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n    for (Book b : results) sb.append(b.getTitle()).append(\"; \");\n    System.out.println(\"Search \" + label + \" -> \" + sb);\n  }\n}","output":"== 1. Search ==\nSearch 'martin' -> Clean Code; Refactoring; \nSearch ISBN 9780441172719 -> Dune; \nSearch 'CLEAN' -> Clean Code; \n\n== 2. Check out with a 14-day due date ==\nAlice borrowed Clean Code on 2026-01-05, due 2026-01-19\nBob borrowed the second copy; Clean Code available copies = 0\nCarol refused: No copy of 'Clean Code' is available\n\n== 3. Five-book limit ==\nCarol now holds 5 books\nRefused: Member carol already has 5 books on loan\n\n== 4. Two members race for the last copy ==\nDesign Patterns: winners=1, losers=1, available=0\n\n== 5. Fines on late returns ==\nAlice returns Clean Code 6 days late: fine $3.00\nBob returns 36 days late: fine $10.00 (capped at $10.00)\nPriya (premium) returns 20 days late: fine $5.00 (half of $10.00 cap)\nBob returns on time: fine $0.00\n\n== 6. Reservations ==\nCannot reserve: A copy of 'Refactoring' is available; borrow it instead\nWaiting for Dune: 2\nAlice returns Dune:\n  [EMAIL] to bob: 'Dune' is now available for you.\n  [SMS] to bob: Your reserved book is ready: Dune\nAlice tries to borrow it again: Remaining copies of 'Dune' are reserved for other members\nBob, first in the queue, borrows Dune\nBob returns Dune:\n  [EMAIL] to priya: 'Dune' is now available for you.\n  [SMS] to priya: Your reserved book is ready: Dune"},"tests":{"file":"Tests.java","cases":["search by title, author and ISBN","due date is 14 days after checkout","member limited to five loans","return frees the copy; double return rejected","single copy never lent twice under 64 concurrent requests","five-loan limit holds under concurrent checkouts by one member","per-day fine, none on the due date","fine rules compose: per-day, cap, member type","reservations are first-come first-served and earmark the copy","reserve rejected while a copy is available","a new notification channel plugs in without changing lending"],"body":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\npublic class Tests {\n  static int passed = 0;\n\n  static void check(boolean cond, String msg) { if (!cond) throw new AssertionError(msg); }\n\n  static void expect(Class<? extends Throwable> type, Runnable r, String msg) {\n    try {\n      r.run();\n    } catch (Throwable t) {\n      if (type.isInstance(t)) return;\n      throw new AssertionError(msg + \" (threw \" + t + \")\");\n    }\n    throw new AssertionError(msg + \" (nothing thrown)\");\n  }\n\n  static void pass(String name) { passed++; System.out.println(\"PASS: \" + name); }\n\n  static Book book(String isbn, String title, String author, int copies) {\n    Book b = new Book(isbn, title, List.of(author));\n    for (int i = 0; i < copies; i++) b.addCopy(isbn + \"-\" + i);\n    return b;\n  }\n\n  static class Env {\n    MutableClock clock = new MutableClock(Instant.parse(\"2026-01-05T09:00:00Z\"));\n    ReservationService reservations = new ReservationService();\n    List<String> notices = new ArrayList<>();\n    FineCalculator fines = new PerDayFine(Money.ofCents(50));\n    LendingService lending;\n\n    Env() { reservations.addListener((m, b) -> notices.add(m.getId() + \":\" + b.getTitle())); }\n\n    LendingService lending() {\n      if (lending == null) lending = new LendingService(clock, fines, reservations);\n      return lending;\n    }\n  }\n\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    Catalog catalog = new Catalog();\n    catalog.add(book(\"111\", \"Clean Code\", \"Robert C. Martin\", 1));\n    catalog.add(book(\"222\", \"Refactoring\", \"Martin Fowler\", 1));\n    check(catalog.search(\"martin\").size() == 2, \"author search matches both books\");\n    check(catalog.search(\"clean\").size() == 1, \"title search is case-insensitive\");\n    check(catalog.search(\"222\").get(0).getTitle().equals(\"Refactoring\"), \"ISBN search\");\n    check(catalog.search(\"zzz\").isEmpty(), \"no match returns empty list\");\n    pass(\"search by title, author and ISBN\");\n\n    Env e = new Env();\n    Book b = book(\"333\", \"Dune\", \"Frank Herbert\", 1);\n    Member m = new Member(\"m1\", \"M\");\n    Loan loan = e.lending().checkOut(m, b);\n    check(loan.getDueOn().equals(LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 19)), \"due date is 14 days out\");\n    check(!b.findAllCopies().get(0).isAvailable(), \"copy marked on loan\");\n    pass(\"due date is 14 days after checkout\");\n\n    Env lim = new Env();\n    Member heavy = new Member(\"heavy\", \"H\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) lim.lending().checkOut(heavy, book(\"L\" + i, \"T\" + i, \"A\", 1));\n    expect(LoanLimitException.class, () -> lim.lending().checkOut(heavy, book(\"L9\", \"T9\", \"A\", 1)), \"6th loan rejected\");\n    check(heavy.activeLoanCount() == 5, \"still five loans\");\n    pass(\"member limited to five loans\");\n\n    Env ret = new Env();\n    Book rb = book(\"R1\", \"Return Me\", \"A\", 1);\n    Member rm = new Member(\"rm\", \"R\");\n    Loan rl = ret.lending().checkOut(rm, rb);\n    ret.lending().returnCopy(rl);\n    check(rb.availableCount() == 1 && rm.activeLoanCount() == 0, \"returning frees copy and member slot\");\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> ret.lending().returnCopy(rl), \"double return rejected\");\n    ret.lending().checkOut(rm, rb);\n    pass(\"return frees the copy; double return rejected\");\n\n    Env race = new Env();\n    Book one = book(\"RACE\", \"One Copy\", \"A\", 1);\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(32);\n    CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    AtomicInteger ok = new AtomicInteger();\n    List<Future<?>> fs = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < 64; i++) {\n      Member mem = new Member(\"racer\" + i, \"R\" + i);\n      fs.add(pool.submit(() -> {\n        try {\n          go.await();\n          race.lending().checkOut(mem, one);\n          ok.incrementAndGet();\n        } catch (NoCopyAvailableException ignored) {\n        } catch (InterruptedException ignored) { }\n      }));\n    }\n    go.countDown();\n    for (Future<?> f : fs) f.get();\n    pool.shutdown();\n    check(ok.get() == 1, \"exactly one of 64 threads gets the single copy, got \" + ok.get());\n    pass(\"single copy never lent twice under 64 concurrent requests\");\n\n    Env multi = new Env();\n    Member busy = new Member(\"busy\", \"B\");\n    Book[] many = new Book[40];\n    for (int i = 0; i < 40; i++) many[i] = book(\"M\" + i, \"M\" + i, \"A\", 1);\n    ExecutorService pool2 = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(16);\n    AtomicInteger borrowed = new AtomicInteger();\n    List<Future<?>> fs2 = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (Book bk : many) fs2.add(pool2.submit(() -> {\n      try {\n        multi.lending().checkOut(busy, bk);\n        borrowed.incrementAndGet();\n      } catch (LoanLimitException ignored) { }\n    }));\n    for (Future<?> f : fs2) f.get();\n    pool2.shutdown();\n    check(borrowed.get() == 5 && busy.activeLoanCount() == 5, \"limit holds when one member borrows concurrently, got \" + borrowed.get());\n    pass(\"five-loan limit holds under concurrent checkouts by one member\");\n\n    Env f = new Env();\n    Book fb = book(\"F1\", \"Fine Book\", \"A\", 3);\n    Member fm = new Member(\"fm\", \"F\");\n    Loan l1 = f.lending().checkOut(fm, fb);\n    f.clock.advance(Duration.ofDays(14));\n    check(f.lending().returnCopy(l1).equals(Money.ZERO), \"returned on the due date: no fine\");\n    Loan l2 = f.lending().checkOut(fm, fb);\n    f.clock.advance(Duration.ofDays(17));\n    check(f.lending().returnCopy(l2).equals(Money.ofCents(150)), \"3 days late at $0.50 = $1.50\");\n    pass(\"per-day fine, none on the due date\");\n\n    FineCalculator capped = new CappedFine(new PerDayFine(Money.ofCents(50)), Money.dollars(10));\n    FineCalculator tiered = new MemberTypeFine(capped, 50);\n    Env g = new Env();\n    g.fines = tiered;\n    Book gb = book(\"G1\", \"G\", \"A\", 2);\n    Member std = new Member(\"std\", \"S\");\n    Member prem = new Member(\"prem\", \"P\", MemberType.PREMIUM);\n    Loan ls = g.lending().checkOut(std, gb);\n    Loan lp = g.lending().checkOut(prem, gb);\n    g.clock.advance(Duration.ofDays(14 + 60));\n    check(g.lending().returnCopy(ls).equals(Money.dollars(10)), \"standard member fine capped at $10\");\n    check(g.lending().returnCopy(lp).equals(Money.dollars(5)), \"premium member pays half of capped fine\");\n    pass(\"fine rules compose: per-day, cap, member type\");\n\n    Env r = new Env();\n    Book rd = book(\"RD\", \"Hot Title\", \"A\", 1);\n    Member a = new Member(\"a\", \"A\"), bb = new Member(\"b\", \"B\"), c = new Member(\"c\", \"C\");\n    Loan al = r.lending().checkOut(a, rd);\n    r.reservations.reserve(bb, rd);\n    r.reservations.reserve(c, rd);\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> r.reservations.reserve(bb, rd), \"duplicate reservation rejected\");\n    r.lending().returnCopy(al);\n    check(r.notices.equals(List.of(\"b:Hot Title\")), \"only the first waiter is notified: \" + r.notices);\n    expect(NoCopyAvailableException.class, () -> r.lending().checkOut(c, rd), \"copy earmarked for first waiter\");\n    Loan bl = r.lending().checkOut(bb, rd);\n    r.lending().returnCopy(bl);\n    check(r.notices.equals(List.of(\"b:Hot Title\", \"c:Hot Title\")), \"second waiter notified on next return: \" + r.notices);\n    pass(\"reservations are first-come first-served and earmark the copy\");\n\n    Env avail = new Env();\n    Book free = book(\"FREE\", \"Plenty\", \"A\", 2);\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> avail.reservations.reserve(new Member(\"x\", \"X\"), free), \"cannot reserve an available title\");\n    pass(\"reserve rejected while a copy is available\");\n\n    Env ext = new Env();\n    List<String> pushes = new ArrayList<>();\n    ext.reservations.addListener((who, bk) -> pushes.add(\"push:\" + who.getId()));\n    Book eb = book(\"EXT\", \"Ext\", \"A\", 1);\n    Member e1 = new Member(\"e1\", \"E1\"), e2 = new Member(\"e2\", \"E2\");\n    Loan el = ext.lending().checkOut(e1, eb);\n    ext.reservations.reserve(e2, eb);\n    ext.lending().returnCopy(el);\n    check(pushes.equals(List.of(\"push:e2\")) && ext.notices.size() == 1, \"new channel added without touching the loan flow\");\n    pass(\"a new notification channel plugs in without changing lending\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"All \" + passed + \" tests passed\");\n  }\n}","output":"PASS: search by title, author and ISBN\nPASS: due date is 14 days after checkout\nPASS: member limited to five loans\nPASS: return frees the copy; double return rejected\nPASS: single copy never lent twice under 64 concurrent requests\nPASS: five-loan limit holds under concurrent checkouts by one member\nPASS: per-day fine, none on the due date\nPASS: fine rules compose: per-day, cap, member type\nPASS: reservations are first-come first-served and earmark the copy\nPASS: reserve rejected while a copy is available\nPASS: a new notification channel plugs in without changing lending\nAll 11 tests passed"},"complexity":["Search: O(B) over B titles, plus sorting the matches.","Check out: O(C) over the copies of one title, under that title's lock.","Return: O(1) plus the fine rule; promoting the next waiter is O(1).","Reserve: O(W) for the duplicate check on W waiting members."]});
window.SOLUTIONS.push({"id":"social-network","intro":"Four ideas drive this design: users with symmetric friendships, content as posts with a tree of comments, a feed whose ordering is a pluggable strategy, and notifications published as events. `SocialNetwork` is a thin facade that checks visibility and publishes events, so the domain classes stay free of those concerns. Every file compiles together with plain `javac`; the demo output and test results below are from a real run.","steps":[{"title":"Requirements 1 and 2: users and mutual friendships","text":"A friendship is symmetric, so accepting a request adds each user to the other's friend set. `FriendRequest` has its own tiny lifecycle: `resolve` succeeds only while the request is `PENDING`, which is what stops two threads accepting the same request. `FriendshipService.send` runs in one critical section so two crossing requests (A to B and B to A at the same moment) cannot both be created, and `accept` checks that the caller really is the recipient.","code":[{"file":"User.java","body":"import java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\npublic class User {\n  private final String id;\n  private final String name;\n  private final Set<String> friendIds = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n\n  public User(String id, String name) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.name = name;\n  }\n\n  void addFriend(String otherId) { friendIds.add(otherId); }\n  public boolean isFriendsWith(String otherId) { return friendIds.contains(otherId); }\n  public Set<String> getFriendIds() { return Set.copyOf(friendIds); }\n\n  public String getId() { return id; }\n  public String getName() { return name; }\n}"},{"file":"FriendRequest.java","body":"public class FriendRequest {\n  public enum Status { PENDING, ACCEPTED, DECLINED }\n\n  private final String fromId;\n  private final String toId;\n  private Status status = Status.PENDING;\n\n  public FriendRequest(String fromId, String toId) {\n    this.fromId = fromId;\n    this.toId = toId;\n  }\n\n  // Only a PENDING request can be resolved, and only once.\n  synchronized boolean resolve(Status next) {\n    if (status != Status.PENDING) return false;\n    status = next;\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized Status getStatus() { return status; }\n  public String getFromId() { return fromId; }\n  public String getToId() { return toId; }\n}"},{"file":"FriendshipService.java","body":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class FriendshipService {\n  private final Map<String, User> users;\n  private final NotificationService notifications;\n  private final Map<String, FriendRequest> pending = new HashMap<>();   // key \"from>to\"\n\n  public FriendshipService(Map<String, User> users, NotificationService notifications) {\n    this.users = users;\n    this.notifications = notifications;\n  }\n\n  public FriendRequest send(String fromId, String toId) {\n    FriendRequest r;\n    synchronized (this) {\n      User from = require(fromId);\n      require(toId);\n      if (fromId.equals(toId)) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Cannot friend yourself\");\n      if (from.isFriendsWith(toId)) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Already friends\");\n      if (pending.containsKey(fromId + \">\" + toId) || pending.containsKey(toId + \">\" + fromId))\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"A request between these users is already pending\");\n      r = new FriendRequest(fromId, toId);\n      pending.put(fromId + \">\" + toId, r);\n    }\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.FRIEND_REQUEST, fromId, toId, 0));\n    return r;\n  }\n\n  public void accept(FriendRequest r, String byUserId) {\n    if (!byUserId.equals(r.getToId())) throw new SecurityException(\"Only the recipient can accept\");\n    if (!r.resolve(FriendRequest.Status.ACCEPTED)) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Request already handled\");\n    users.get(r.getFromId()).addFriend(r.getToId());\n    users.get(r.getToId()).addFriend(r.getFromId());      // friendship is mutual\n    clear(r);\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.FRIEND_ACCEPTED, r.getToId(), r.getFromId(), 0));\n  }\n\n  public void decline(FriendRequest r, String byUserId) {\n    if (!byUserId.equals(r.getToId())) throw new SecurityException(\"Only the recipient can decline\");\n    if (!r.resolve(FriendRequest.Status.DECLINED)) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Request already handled\");\n    clear(r);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized List<FriendRequest> pendingFor(String userId) {\n    List<FriendRequest> out = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (FriendRequest r : pending.values()) if (r.getToId().equals(userId)) out.add(r);\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  private synchronized void clear(FriendRequest r) { pending.remove(r.getFromId() + \">\" + r.getToId()); }\n\n  private User require(String id) {\n    User u = users.get(id);\n    if (u == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Unknown user \" + id);\n    return u;\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 3: posts and visibility","text":"Visibility is a rule on the post: public is visible to anyone; friends-only to the author and the author's friends. Because the rule lives in `Post.isVisibleTo`, the feed, comment and reaction code all share the same answer. The facade calls `requireVisible` before it lets anyone comment or react, so a stranger cannot interact with a friends-only post.","code":[{"file":"Visibility.java","body":"public enum Visibility { PUBLIC, FRIENDS_ONLY }"},{"file":"Post.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class Post {\n  private final long id;\n  private final User author;\n  private final String text;\n  private final Visibility visibility;\n  private final Instant createdAt;\n  private final Map<String, ReactionType> reactions = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n  private final List<Comment> comments = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public Post(long id, User author, String text, Visibility visibility, Instant createdAt) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.author = author;\n    this.text = text;\n    this.visibility = visibility;\n    this.createdAt = createdAt;\n  }\n\n  public boolean isVisibleTo(User viewer) {\n    if (visibility == Visibility.PUBLIC) return true;\n    return viewer.getId().equals(author.getId()) || author.isFriendsWith(viewer.getId());\n  }\n\n  // One reaction per user: a later call replaces the earlier one. Returns true if anything changed.\n  public boolean react(String userId, ReactionType type) {\n    return reactions.put(userId, type) != type;\n  }\n\n  public void removeReaction(String userId) { reactions.remove(userId); }\n\n  public void addComment(Comment c) { comments.add(c); }\n\n  public int reactionCount() { return reactions.size(); }\n  public int commentCount() { return comments.stream().mapToInt(Comment::totalCount).sum(); }\n\n  public Map<ReactionType, Long> reactionBreakdown() {\n    Map<ReactionType, Long> out = new EnumMap<>(ReactionType.class);\n    for (ReactionType t : reactions.values()) out.merge(t, 1L, Long::sum);\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  public long getId() { return id; }\n  public User getAuthor() { return author; }\n  public String getText() { return text; }\n  public Visibility getVisibility() { return visibility; }\n  public Instant getCreatedAt() { return createdAt; }\n  public List<Comment> getComments() { return comments; }\n}"},{"file":"PostRepository.java","body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class PostRepository {\n  private final Map<String, List<Post>> byAuthor = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n  public void add(Post p) {\n    byAuthor.computeIfAbsent(p.getAuthor().getId(), k -> new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>()).add(p);\n  }\n\n  public List<Post> byAuthors(Set<String> authorIds) {\n    List<Post> out = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (String id : authorIds) out.addAll(byAuthor.getOrDefault(id, List.of()));\n    return out;\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 4: nested comments as a tree","text":"A comment can contain comments, and callers treat one comment and a whole thread the same way. That is a tree, so `Comment` holds its replies directly and `totalCount` recurses. Replies live in a `CopyOnWriteArrayList`, so concurrent replies are never lost.","code":[{"file":"Comment.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class Comment {\n  private final long id;\n  private final String authorId;\n  private final String text;\n  private final Instant createdAt;\n  private final List<Comment> replies = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public Comment(long id, String authorId, String text, Instant createdAt) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.authorId = authorId;\n    this.text = text;\n    this.createdAt = createdAt;\n  }\n\n  public Comment reply(long id, String authorId, String text, Instant at) {\n    Comment c = new Comment(id, authorId, text, at);\n    replies.add(c);\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  // Same call works on a leaf and on a whole thread.\n  public int totalCount() {\n    int n = 1;\n    for (Comment r : replies) n += r.totalCount();\n    return n;\n  }\n\n  public long getId() { return id; }\n  public String getAuthorId() { return authorId; }\n  public String getText() { return text; }\n  public List<Comment> getReplies() { return replies; }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 5: reactions, one per user","text":"A map keyed by user id enforces the rule naturally: putting a second reaction for the same user replaces the first. `react` returns whether anything changed so the facade can skip a notification when someone taps the same reaction twice. `ConcurrentHashMap` makes concurrent reactions safe without an explicit lock.","code":[{"file":"ReactionType.java","body":"public enum ReactionType { LIKE, LOVE, LAUGH }"},{"file":"Post.java  ›  react","body":"// One reaction per user: a later call replaces the earlier one. Returns true if anything changed.\npublic boolean react(String userId, ReactionType type) {\n  return reactions.put(userId, type) != type;\n}"},{"file":"SocialNetwork.java  ›  react (facade)","body":"public void react(User by, Post post, ReactionType type) {\n  requireVisible(by, post);\n  if (post.react(by.getId(), type))     // only notify when the reaction actually changed\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.REACTION, by.getId(), post.getAuthor().getId(), post.getId()));\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 6: the feed, with pluggable ranking","text":"Feed assembly has two separate jobs and the code keeps them apart. `FeedService` decides what the viewer may see (friends' posts that pass the visibility rule). A `FeedRanker` only decides the order. Switching from chronological to engagement ranking is a call to `setRanker`, and the assembly code does not change.","code":[{"file":"FeedRanker.java","body":"import java.util.List;\n\npublic interface FeedRanker {\n  List<Post> rank(User viewer, List<Post> candidates);\n}"},{"file":"ChronologicalRanker.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class ChronologicalRanker implements FeedRanker {\n  public List<Post> rank(User viewer, List<Post> candidates) {\n    List<Post> out = new ArrayList<>(candidates);\n    out.sort(Comparator.comparing(Post::getCreatedAt).reversed());\n    return out;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"EngagementRanker.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class EngagementRanker implements FeedRanker {\n  private final Clock clock;\n\n  public EngagementRanker(Clock clock) { this.clock = clock; }\n\n  public List<Post> rank(User viewer, List<Post> candidates) {\n    Instant now = clock.instant();\n    List<Post> out = new ArrayList<>(candidates);\n    out.sort(Comparator.comparingDouble((Post p) -> score(p, now)).reversed());\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  // Comments count double; older posts decay.\n  private double score(Post p, Instant now) {\n    long ageHours = Duration.between(p.getCreatedAt(), now).toHours();\n    return (p.reactionCount() + 2.0 * p.commentCount()) / (1.0 + ageHours);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"FeedService.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.stream.Collectors;\n\npublic class FeedService {\n  private final PostRepository posts;\n  private final Map<String, User> users;\n  private volatile FeedRanker ranker;\n\n  public FeedService(PostRepository posts, Map<String, User> users, FeedRanker ranker) {\n    this.posts = posts;\n    this.users = users;\n    this.ranker = ranker;\n  }\n\n  public void setRanker(FeedRanker ranker) { this.ranker = ranker; }\n\n  // Step 1 chooses what the viewer may see; step 2 (the ranker) only decides the order.\n  public List<Post> feedFor(String viewerId, int limit) {\n    User viewer = users.get(viewerId);\n    List<Post> candidates = posts.byAuthors(viewer.getFriendIds()).stream()\n        .filter(p -> p.isVisibleTo(viewer))\n        .collect(Collectors.toList());\n    return ranker.rank(viewer, candidates).stream().limit(limit).collect(Collectors.toList());\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"Extensibility: notifications through events","text":"Posting, reacting and commenting do not know who is listening. They publish an `ActivityEvent`; each subscriber decides what to do with it. An in-app inbox and a push channel are two subscribers, and a new channel is one new class. `NotificationService` catches subscriber failures so a broken channel cannot block a post.","code":[{"file":"ActivityEvent.java","body":"public record ActivityEvent(Type type, String actorId, String targetUserId, long postId) {\n  public enum Type { FRIEND_REQUEST, FRIEND_ACCEPTED, REACTION, COMMENT }\n\n  public String message(String actorName) {\n    switch (type) {\n      case FRIEND_REQUEST:  return actorName + \" sent you a friend request\";\n      case FRIEND_ACCEPTED: return actorName + \" accepted your friend request\";\n      case REACTION:        return actorName + \" reacted to your post\";\n      default:              return actorName + \" commented on your post\";\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"NotificationService.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class NotificationService {\n  @FunctionalInterface\n  public interface Subscriber { void onEvent(ActivityEvent event); }\n\n  private final List<Subscriber> subscribers = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public void subscribe(Subscriber s) { subscribers.add(s); }\n\n  public void publish(ActivityEvent e) {\n    for (Subscriber s : subscribers) {\n      try {\n        s.onEvent(e);\n      } catch (RuntimeException ex) {\n        // One broken channel must not stop the post or the other channels.\n        System.err.println(\"Subscriber failed: \" + ex);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"InAppSubscriber.java","body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class InAppSubscriber implements NotificationService.Subscriber {\n  private final Map<String, User> users;\n  private final Map<String, List<String>> inboxes = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n  public InAppSubscriber(Map<String, User> users) { this.users = users; }\n\n  public void onEvent(ActivityEvent e) {\n    if (e.targetUserId() == null || e.targetUserId().equals(e.actorId())) return;\n    inboxes.computeIfAbsent(e.targetUserId(), k -> new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>())\n        .add(e.message(users.get(e.actorId()).getName()));\n  }\n\n  public List<String> inbox(String userId) { return inboxes.getOrDefault(userId, List.of()); }\n}"},{"file":"PushClient.java","body":"@FunctionalInterface\npublic interface PushClient {\n  void send(String userId, String text);\n}"},{"file":"PushSubscriber.java","body":"import java.util.Map;\n\npublic class PushSubscriber implements NotificationService.Subscriber {\n  private final Map<String, User> users;\n  private final PushClient push;\n\n  public PushSubscriber(Map<String, User> users, PushClient push) {\n    this.users = users;\n    this.push = push;\n  }\n\n  public void onEvent(ActivityEvent e) {\n    if (e.targetUserId() == null || e.targetUserId().equals(e.actorId())) return;  // never notify yourself\n    push.send(e.targetUserId(), e.message(users.get(e.actorId()).getName()));\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"The facade","text":"`SocialNetwork` is the single entry point. It creates ids, checks visibility, mutates the domain objects and publishes events, so each domain class has one job.","code":[{"file":"SocialNetwork.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\n// Facade: the one place that checks visibility and publishes events.\npublic class SocialNetwork {\n  private final Clock clock;\n  private final AtomicLong ids = new AtomicLong();\n  private final Map<String, User> users = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n  private final NotificationService notifications = new NotificationService();\n  private final FriendshipService friendships = new FriendshipService(users, notifications);\n  private final PostRepository posts = new PostRepository();\n  private final FeedService feed;\n\n  public SocialNetwork(Clock clock, FeedRanker ranker) {\n    this.clock = clock;\n    this.feed = new FeedService(posts, users, ranker);\n  }\n\n  public User register(String name) {\n    User u = new User(\"u\" + ids.incrementAndGet(), name);\n    users.put(u.getId(), u);\n    return u;\n  }\n\n  public Post post(User author, String text, Visibility visibility) {\n    Post p = new Post(ids.incrementAndGet(), author, text, visibility, clock.instant());\n    posts.add(p);\n    return p;\n  }\n\n  public Comment comment(User by, Post post, String text) {\n    requireVisible(by, post);\n    Comment c = new Comment(ids.incrementAndGet(), by.getId(), text, clock.instant());\n    post.addComment(c);\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.COMMENT, by.getId(), post.getAuthor().getId(), post.getId()));\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  public Comment reply(User by, Post post, Comment parent, String text) {\n    requireVisible(by, post);\n    Comment c = parent.reply(ids.incrementAndGet(), by.getId(), text, clock.instant());\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.COMMENT, by.getId(), post.getAuthor().getId(), post.getId()));\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  public void react(User by, Post post, ReactionType type) {\n    requireVisible(by, post);\n    if (post.react(by.getId(), type))     // only notify when the reaction actually changed\n      notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.REACTION, by.getId(), post.getAuthor().getId(), post.getId()));\n  }\n\n  public void unreact(User by, Post post) { post.removeReaction(by.getId()); }\n\n  private void requireVisible(User viewer, Post post) {\n    if (!post.isVisibleTo(viewer)) throw new SecurityException(viewer.getName() + \" cannot see this post\");\n  }\n\n  public Map<String, User> users() { return users; }\n  public FriendshipService friendships() { return friendships; }\n  public NotificationService notifications() { return notifications; }\n  public FeedService feed() { return feed; }\n}"}]}],"files":[{"file":"MutableClock.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.time.ZoneId;\nimport java.time.ZoneOffset;\n\n// A clock we can move forward, so feed ordering can be shown and tested without waiting.\npublic class MutableClock extends Clock {\n  private Instant now;\n\n  public MutableClock(Instant start) { this.now = start; }\n\n  public synchronized void advance(Duration d) { now = now.plus(d); }\n\n  @Override public ZoneId getZone() { return ZoneOffset.UTC; }\n  @Override public Clock withZone(ZoneId zone) { return this; }\n  @Override public synchronized Instant instant() { return now; }\n}"},{"file":"User.java","body":"import java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\npublic class User {\n  private final String id;\n  private final String name;\n  private final Set<String> friendIds = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n\n  public User(String id, String name) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.name = name;\n  }\n\n  void addFriend(String otherId) { friendIds.add(otherId); }\n  public boolean isFriendsWith(String otherId) { return friendIds.contains(otherId); }\n  public Set<String> getFriendIds() { return Set.copyOf(friendIds); }\n\n  public String getId() { return id; }\n  public String getName() { return name; }\n}"},{"file":"FriendRequest.java","body":"public class FriendRequest {\n  public enum Status { PENDING, ACCEPTED, DECLINED }\n\n  private final String fromId;\n  private final String toId;\n  private Status status = Status.PENDING;\n\n  public FriendRequest(String fromId, String toId) {\n    this.fromId = fromId;\n    this.toId = toId;\n  }\n\n  // Only a PENDING request can be resolved, and only once.\n  synchronized boolean resolve(Status next) {\n    if (status != Status.PENDING) return false;\n    status = next;\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized Status getStatus() { return status; }\n  public String getFromId() { return fromId; }\n  public String getToId() { return toId; }\n}"},{"file":"ActivityEvent.java","body":"public record ActivityEvent(Type type, String actorId, String targetUserId, long postId) {\n  public enum Type { FRIEND_REQUEST, FRIEND_ACCEPTED, REACTION, COMMENT }\n\n  public String message(String actorName) {\n    switch (type) {\n      case FRIEND_REQUEST:  return actorName + \" sent you a friend request\";\n      case FRIEND_ACCEPTED: return actorName + \" accepted your friend request\";\n      case REACTION:        return actorName + \" reacted to your post\";\n      default:              return actorName + \" commented on your post\";\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"NotificationService.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class NotificationService {\n  @FunctionalInterface\n  public interface Subscriber { void onEvent(ActivityEvent event); }\n\n  private final List<Subscriber> subscribers = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public void subscribe(Subscriber s) { subscribers.add(s); }\n\n  public void publish(ActivityEvent e) {\n    for (Subscriber s : subscribers) {\n      try {\n        s.onEvent(e);\n      } catch (RuntimeException ex) {\n        // One broken channel must not stop the post or the other channels.\n        System.err.println(\"Subscriber failed: \" + ex);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"FriendshipService.java","body":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class FriendshipService {\n  private final Map<String, User> users;\n  private final NotificationService notifications;\n  private final Map<String, FriendRequest> pending = new HashMap<>();   // key \"from>to\"\n\n  public FriendshipService(Map<String, User> users, NotificationService notifications) {\n    this.users = users;\n    this.notifications = notifications;\n  }\n\n  public FriendRequest send(String fromId, String toId) {\n    FriendRequest r;\n    synchronized (this) {\n      User from = require(fromId);\n      require(toId);\n      if (fromId.equals(toId)) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Cannot friend yourself\");\n      if (from.isFriendsWith(toId)) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Already friends\");\n      if (pending.containsKey(fromId + \">\" + toId) || pending.containsKey(toId + \">\" + fromId))\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"A request between these users is already pending\");\n      r = new FriendRequest(fromId, toId);\n      pending.put(fromId + \">\" + toId, r);\n    }\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.FRIEND_REQUEST, fromId, toId, 0));\n    return r;\n  }\n\n  public void accept(FriendRequest r, String byUserId) {\n    if (!byUserId.equals(r.getToId())) throw new SecurityException(\"Only the recipient can accept\");\n    if (!r.resolve(FriendRequest.Status.ACCEPTED)) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Request already handled\");\n    users.get(r.getFromId()).addFriend(r.getToId());\n    users.get(r.getToId()).addFriend(r.getFromId());      // friendship is mutual\n    clear(r);\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.FRIEND_ACCEPTED, r.getToId(), r.getFromId(), 0));\n  }\n\n  public void decline(FriendRequest r, String byUserId) {\n    if (!byUserId.equals(r.getToId())) throw new SecurityException(\"Only the recipient can decline\");\n    if (!r.resolve(FriendRequest.Status.DECLINED)) throw new IllegalStateException(\"Request already handled\");\n    clear(r);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized List<FriendRequest> pendingFor(String userId) {\n    List<FriendRequest> out = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (FriendRequest r : pending.values()) if (r.getToId().equals(userId)) out.add(r);\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  private synchronized void clear(FriendRequest r) { pending.remove(r.getFromId() + \">\" + r.getToId()); }\n\n  private User require(String id) {\n    User u = users.get(id);\n    if (u == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Unknown user \" + id);\n    return u;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"Visibility.java","body":"public enum Visibility { PUBLIC, FRIENDS_ONLY }"},{"file":"ReactionType.java","body":"public enum ReactionType { LIKE, LOVE, LAUGH }"},{"file":"Comment.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class Comment {\n  private final long id;\n  private final String authorId;\n  private final String text;\n  private final Instant createdAt;\n  private final List<Comment> replies = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public Comment(long id, String authorId, String text, Instant createdAt) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.authorId = authorId;\n    this.text = text;\n    this.createdAt = createdAt;\n  }\n\n  public Comment reply(long id, String authorId, String text, Instant at) {\n    Comment c = new Comment(id, authorId, text, at);\n    replies.add(c);\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  // Same call works on a leaf and on a whole thread.\n  public int totalCount() {\n    int n = 1;\n    for (Comment r : replies) n += r.totalCount();\n    return n;\n  }\n\n  public long getId() { return id; }\n  public String getAuthorId() { return authorId; }\n  public String getText() { return text; }\n  public List<Comment> getReplies() { return replies; }\n}"},{"file":"Post.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class Post {\n  private final long id;\n  private final User author;\n  private final String text;\n  private final Visibility visibility;\n  private final Instant createdAt;\n  private final Map<String, ReactionType> reactions = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n  private final List<Comment> comments = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public Post(long id, User author, String text, Visibility visibility, Instant createdAt) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.author = author;\n    this.text = text;\n    this.visibility = visibility;\n    this.createdAt = createdAt;\n  }\n\n  public boolean isVisibleTo(User viewer) {\n    if (visibility == Visibility.PUBLIC) return true;\n    return viewer.getId().equals(author.getId()) || author.isFriendsWith(viewer.getId());\n  }\n\n  // One reaction per user: a later call replaces the earlier one. Returns true if anything changed.\n  public boolean react(String userId, ReactionType type) {\n    return reactions.put(userId, type) != type;\n  }\n\n  public void removeReaction(String userId) { reactions.remove(userId); }\n\n  public void addComment(Comment c) { comments.add(c); }\n\n  public int reactionCount() { return reactions.size(); }\n  public int commentCount() { return comments.stream().mapToInt(Comment::totalCount).sum(); }\n\n  public Map<ReactionType, Long> reactionBreakdown() {\n    Map<ReactionType, Long> out = new EnumMap<>(ReactionType.class);\n    for (ReactionType t : reactions.values()) out.merge(t, 1L, Long::sum);\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  public long getId() { return id; }\n  public User getAuthor() { return author; }\n  public String getText() { return text; }\n  public Visibility getVisibility() { return visibility; }\n  public Instant getCreatedAt() { return createdAt; }\n  public List<Comment> getComments() { return comments; }\n}"},{"file":"PostRepository.java","body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class PostRepository {\n  private final Map<String, List<Post>> byAuthor = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n  public void add(Post p) {\n    byAuthor.computeIfAbsent(p.getAuthor().getId(), k -> new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>()).add(p);\n  }\n\n  public List<Post> byAuthors(Set<String> authorIds) {\n    List<Post> out = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (String id : authorIds) out.addAll(byAuthor.getOrDefault(id, List.of()));\n    return out;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"FeedRanker.java","body":"import java.util.List;\n\npublic interface FeedRanker {\n  List<Post> rank(User viewer, List<Post> candidates);\n}"},{"file":"ChronologicalRanker.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class ChronologicalRanker implements FeedRanker {\n  public List<Post> rank(User viewer, List<Post> candidates) {\n    List<Post> out = new ArrayList<>(candidates);\n    out.sort(Comparator.comparing(Post::getCreatedAt).reversed());\n    return out;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"EngagementRanker.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class EngagementRanker implements FeedRanker {\n  private final Clock clock;\n\n  public EngagementRanker(Clock clock) { this.clock = clock; }\n\n  public List<Post> rank(User viewer, List<Post> candidates) {\n    Instant now = clock.instant();\n    List<Post> out = new ArrayList<>(candidates);\n    out.sort(Comparator.comparingDouble((Post p) -> score(p, now)).reversed());\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  // Comments count double; older posts decay.\n  private double score(Post p, Instant now) {\n    long ageHours = Duration.between(p.getCreatedAt(), now).toHours();\n    return (p.reactionCount() + 2.0 * p.commentCount()) / (1.0 + ageHours);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"FeedService.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.stream.Collectors;\n\npublic class FeedService {\n  private final PostRepository posts;\n  private final Map<String, User> users;\n  private volatile FeedRanker ranker;\n\n  public FeedService(PostRepository posts, Map<String, User> users, FeedRanker ranker) {\n    this.posts = posts;\n    this.users = users;\n    this.ranker = ranker;\n  }\n\n  public void setRanker(FeedRanker ranker) { this.ranker = ranker; }\n\n  // Step 1 chooses what the viewer may see; step 2 (the ranker) only decides the order.\n  public List<Post> feedFor(String viewerId, int limit) {\n    User viewer = users.get(viewerId);\n    List<Post> candidates = posts.byAuthors(viewer.getFriendIds()).stream()\n        .filter(p -> p.isVisibleTo(viewer))\n        .collect(Collectors.toList());\n    return ranker.rank(viewer, candidates).stream().limit(limit).collect(Collectors.toList());\n  }\n}"},{"file":"PushClient.java","body":"@FunctionalInterface\npublic interface PushClient {\n  void send(String userId, String text);\n}"},{"file":"PushSubscriber.java","body":"import java.util.Map;\n\npublic class PushSubscriber implements NotificationService.Subscriber {\n  private final Map<String, User> users;\n  private final PushClient push;\n\n  public PushSubscriber(Map<String, User> users, PushClient push) {\n    this.users = users;\n    this.push = push;\n  }\n\n  public void onEvent(ActivityEvent e) {\n    if (e.targetUserId() == null || e.targetUserId().equals(e.actorId())) return;  // never notify yourself\n    push.send(e.targetUserId(), e.message(users.get(e.actorId()).getName()));\n  }\n}"},{"file":"InAppSubscriber.java","body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class InAppSubscriber implements NotificationService.Subscriber {\n  private final Map<String, User> users;\n  private final Map<String, List<String>> inboxes = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n  public InAppSubscriber(Map<String, User> users) { this.users = users; }\n\n  public void onEvent(ActivityEvent e) {\n    if (e.targetUserId() == null || e.targetUserId().equals(e.actorId())) return;\n    inboxes.computeIfAbsent(e.targetUserId(), k -> new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>())\n        .add(e.message(users.get(e.actorId()).getName()));\n  }\n\n  public List<String> inbox(String userId) { return inboxes.getOrDefault(userId, List.of()); }\n}"},{"file":"SocialNetwork.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\n// Facade: the one place that checks visibility and publishes events.\npublic class SocialNetwork {\n  private final Clock clock;\n  private final AtomicLong ids = new AtomicLong();\n  private final Map<String, User> users = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n  private final NotificationService notifications = new NotificationService();\n  private final FriendshipService friendships = new FriendshipService(users, notifications);\n  private final PostRepository posts = new PostRepository();\n  private final FeedService feed;\n\n  public SocialNetwork(Clock clock, FeedRanker ranker) {\n    this.clock = clock;\n    this.feed = new FeedService(posts, users, ranker);\n  }\n\n  public User register(String name) {\n    User u = new User(\"u\" + ids.incrementAndGet(), name);\n    users.put(u.getId(), u);\n    return u;\n  }\n\n  public Post post(User author, String text, Visibility visibility) {\n    Post p = new Post(ids.incrementAndGet(), author, text, visibility, clock.instant());\n    posts.add(p);\n    return p;\n  }\n\n  public Comment comment(User by, Post post, String text) {\n    requireVisible(by, post);\n    Comment c = new Comment(ids.incrementAndGet(), by.getId(), text, clock.instant());\n    post.addComment(c);\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.COMMENT, by.getId(), post.getAuthor().getId(), post.getId()));\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  public Comment reply(User by, Post post, Comment parent, String text) {\n    requireVisible(by, post);\n    Comment c = parent.reply(ids.incrementAndGet(), by.getId(), text, clock.instant());\n    notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.COMMENT, by.getId(), post.getAuthor().getId(), post.getId()));\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  public void react(User by, Post post, ReactionType type) {\n    requireVisible(by, post);\n    if (post.react(by.getId(), type))     // only notify when the reaction actually changed\n      notifications.publish(new ActivityEvent(ActivityEvent.Type.REACTION, by.getId(), post.getAuthor().getId(), post.getId()));\n  }\n\n  public void unreact(User by, Post post) { post.removeReaction(by.getId()); }\n\n  private void requireVisible(User viewer, Post post) {\n    if (!post.isVisibleTo(viewer)) throw new SecurityException(viewer.getName() + \" cannot see this post\");\n  }\n\n  public Map<String, User> users() { return users; }\n  public FriendshipService friendships() { return friendships; }\n  public NotificationService notifications() { return notifications; }\n  public FeedService feed() { return feed; }\n}"}],"driver":{"text":"The demo covers friend requests and their error cases, visibility, feeds, reactions, a nested comment thread, swapping the ranker at runtime, 300 concurrent reactions and comments, and a push channel added after the fact.","file":"Main.java","body":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    MutableClock clock = new MutableClock(Instant.parse(\"2026-03-02T08:00:00Z\"));\n    SocialNetwork net = new SocialNetwork(clock, new ChronologicalRanker());\n    InAppSubscriber inApp = new InAppSubscriber(net.users());\n    net.notifications().subscribe(inApp);\n\n    User alice = net.register(\"Alice\");\n    User bob = net.register(\"Bob\");\n    User carol = net.register(\"Carol\");\n    User dave = net.register(\"Dave\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"== 1. Friend requests ==\");\n    FriendshipService fs = net.friendships();\n    FriendRequest ab = fs.send(alice.getId(), bob.getId());\n    fs.accept(ab, bob.getId());\n    System.out.println(\"Alice and Bob are friends: \" + alice.isFriendsWith(bob.getId()) + \" / \" + bob.isFriendsWith(alice.getId()));\n    FriendRequest bc = fs.send(bob.getId(), carol.getId());\n    fs.accept(bc, carol.getId());\n    FriendRequest ac = fs.send(alice.getId(), carol.getId());\n    fs.decline(ac, carol.getId());\n    System.out.println(\"Carol declined Alice: friends = \" + alice.isFriendsWith(carol.getId()));\n    attempt(\"Alice friends herself\", () -> fs.send(alice.getId(), alice.getId()));\n    attempt(\"Alice re-adds Bob\", () -> fs.send(alice.getId(), bob.getId()));\n    attempt(\"Bob accepts the same request twice\", () -> fs.accept(ab, bob.getId()));\n    FriendRequest dc = fs.send(dave.getId(), carol.getId());\n    attempt(\"Dave accepts his own request\", () -> fs.accept(dc, dave.getId()));\n    attempt(\"Carol sends to Dave while his request is pending\", () -> fs.send(carol.getId(), dave.getId()));\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 2. Posts and visibility ==\");\n    Post hello = net.post(bob, \"Hello world\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofHours(1));\n    Post plans = net.post(bob, \"Weekend plans\", Visibility.FRIENDS_ONLY);\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofHours(1));\n    Post photos = net.post(carol, \"Trip photos\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofHours(1));\n    net.post(dave, \"Dave's public post\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    System.out.println(\"Bob's friends-only post visible to Alice: \" + plans.isVisibleTo(alice));\n    System.out.println(\"Bob's friends-only post visible to Dave:  \" + plans.isVisibleTo(dave));\n    attempt(\"Dave comments on Bob's friends-only post\", () -> net.comment(dave, plans, \"Hi!\"));\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 3. Feeds (chronological) ==\");\n    printFeed(net, alice);\n    printFeed(net, carol);\n    printFeed(net, dave);\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 4. Reactions: one per user ==\");\n    net.react(alice, hello, ReactionType.LIKE);\n    net.react(carol, hello, ReactionType.LIKE);\n    net.react(alice, hello, ReactionType.LOVE);        // replaces Alice's LIKE\n    System.out.println(\"Reactions on 'Hello world': \" + hello.reactionCount() + \" \" + hello.reactionBreakdown());\n    net.unreact(carol, hello);\n    System.out.println(\"After Carol removes hers: \" + hello.reactionCount() + \" \" + hello.reactionBreakdown());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 5. Nested comments ==\");\n    Comment c1 = net.comment(alice, hello, \"Welcome, Bob!\");\n    Comment r1 = net.reply(bob, hello, c1, \"Thanks Alice\");\n    net.reply(carol, hello, r1, \"Agreed\");\n    net.comment(carol, hello, \"First!\");\n    print(hello.getComments(), 0, net);\n    System.out.println(\"Total comments on the post: \" + hello.commentCount());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 6. Swap the ranking without touching feed assembly ==\");\n    net.react(alice, photos, ReactionType.LIKE);\n    net.react(bob, photos, ReactionType.LAUGH);\n    net.comment(bob, photos, \"Wow\");\n    net.feed().setRanker(new EngagementRanker(clock));\n    printFeed(net, alice);   // Alice sees friends' posts: Bob's two (she is not Carol's friend)\n    printFeed(net, bob);\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 7. Concurrent reactions and comments ==\");\n    Post busy = net.post(bob, \"Everyone pile in\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(16);\n    CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    List<Future<?>> fs2 = new java.util.ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < 200; i++) {\n      User fan = net.register(\"fan\" + i);\n      fs2.add(pool.submit(() -> {\n        go.await();\n        net.react(fan, busy, ReactionType.LIKE);\n        net.comment(fan, busy, \"me too\");\n        return null;\n      }));\n    }\n    User eager = net.register(\"eager\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n      final ReactionType t = ReactionType.values()[i % 3];\n      fs2.add(pool.submit(() -> { go.await(); net.react(eager, busy, t); return null; }));\n    }\n    go.countDown();\n    for (Future<?> f : fs2) f.get();\n    pool.shutdown();\n    System.out.println(\"200 fans reacted + commented, and one user reacted 100 times\");\n    System.out.println(\"Reactions: \" + busy.reactionCount() + \" (expected 201), comments: \" + busy.commentCount() + \" (expected 200)\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 8. Notifications (in-app inbox) ==\");\n    System.out.println(\"Bob's inbox, first 6 entries (oldest first):\");\n    inApp.inbox(bob.getId()).stream().limit(6).forEach(m -> System.out.println(\"  - \" + m));\n    System.out.println(\"Alice's inbox: \" + inApp.inbox(alice.getId()));\n    net.notifications().subscribe(new PushSubscriber(net.users(),\n        (userId, text) -> System.out.println(\"    [PUSH] to \" + net.users().get(userId).getName() + \": \" + text)));\n    System.out.println(\"Added a push channel, no posting code changed:\");\n    net.react(carol, plans, ReactionType.LIKE);\n  }\n\n  private static void attempt(String what, Runnable r) {\n    try {\n      r.run();\n      System.out.println(what + \" -> allowed\");\n    } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n      System.out.println(what + \" -> rejected: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n  }\n\n  private static void printFeed(SocialNetwork net, User viewer) {\n    System.out.println(\"Feed for \" + viewer.getName() + \":\");\n    List<Post> feed = net.feed().feedFor(viewer.getId(), 10);\n    if (feed.isEmpty()) System.out.println(\"  (empty)\");\n    for (Post p : feed)\n      System.out.println(\"  - \" + p.getAuthor().getName() + \": \\\"\" + p.getText() + \"\\\" [\" + p.getVisibility()\n          + \", \" + p.reactionCount() + \" reactions, \" + p.commentCount() + \" comments]\");\n  }\n\n  private static void print(List<Comment> comments, int depth, SocialNetwork net) {\n    for (Comment c : comments) {\n      System.out.println(\"  \" + \"  \".repeat(depth) + \"- \" + net.users().get(c.getAuthorId()).getName() + \": \" + c.getText());\n      print(c.getReplies(), depth + 1, net);\n    }\n  }\n}","output":"== 1. Friend requests ==\nAlice and Bob are friends: true / true\nCarol declined Alice: friends = false\nAlice friends herself -> rejected: Cannot friend yourself\nAlice re-adds Bob -> rejected: Already friends\nBob accepts the same request twice -> rejected: Request already handled\nDave accepts his own request -> rejected: Only the recipient can accept\nCarol sends to Dave while his request is pending -> rejected: A request between these users is already pending\n\n== 2. Posts and visibility ==\nBob's friends-only post visible to Alice: true\nBob's friends-only post visible to Dave:  false\nDave comments on Bob's friends-only post -> rejected: Dave cannot see this post\n\n== 3. Feeds (chronological) ==\nFeed for Alice:\n  - Bob: \"Weekend plans\" [FRIENDS_ONLY, 0 reactions, 0 comments]\n  - Bob: \"Hello world\" [PUBLIC, 0 reactions, 0 comments]\nFeed for Carol:\n  - Bob: \"Weekend plans\" [FRIENDS_ONLY, 0 reactions, 0 comments]\n  - Bob: \"Hello world\" [PUBLIC, 0 reactions, 0 comments]\nFeed for Dave:\n  (empty)\n\n== 4. Reactions: one per user ==\nReactions on 'Hello world': 2 {LIKE=1, LOVE=1}\nAfter Carol removes hers: 1 {LOVE=1}\n\n== 5. Nested comments ==\n  - Alice: Welcome, Bob!\n    - Bob: Thanks Alice\n      - Carol: Agreed\n  - Carol: First!\nTotal comments on the post: 4\n\n== 6. Swap the ranking without touching feed assembly ==\nFeed for Alice:\n  - Bob: \"Hello world\" [PUBLIC, 1 reactions, 4 comments]\n  - Bob: \"Weekend plans\" [FRIENDS_ONLY, 0 reactions, 0 comments]\nFeed for Bob:\n  - Carol: \"Trip photos\" [PUBLIC, 2 reactions, 1 comments]\n\n== 7. Concurrent reactions and comments ==\n200 fans reacted + commented, and one user reacted 100 times\nReactions: 201 (expected 201), comments: 200 (expected 200)\n\n== 8. Notifications (in-app inbox) ==\nBob's inbox, first 6 entries (oldest first):\n  - Alice sent you a friend request\n  - Carol accepted your friend request\n  - Alice reacted to your post\n  - Carol reacted to your post\n  - Alice reacted to your post\n  - Alice commented on your post\nAlice's inbox: [Bob accepted your friend request]\nAdded a push channel, no posting code changed:\n    [PUSH] to Bob: Carol reacted to your post"},"tests":{"file":"Tests.java","cases":["accepting a request creates a mutual friendship","friend request validation: self, unknown, duplicate, wrong actor, decline","a request can be accepted only once, even concurrently","crossing friend requests: only one is created","visibility rules are enforced for reading, commenting and reacting","one reaction per user per post; changing replaces, removing clears","nested comments are counted as a tree","no lost reactions or comments under 400 concurrent operations","feed shows friends' visible posts; ranker swapped at runtime","notifications: no self-notices, de-duplicated, extensible, failure-isolated"],"body":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\npublic class Tests {\n  static int passed = 0;\n\n  static void check(boolean cond, String msg) { if (!cond) throw new AssertionError(msg); }\n\n  static void expect(Class<? extends Throwable> type, Runnable r, String msg) {\n    try {\n      r.run();\n    } catch (Throwable t) {\n      if (type.isInstance(t)) return;\n      throw new AssertionError(msg + \" (threw \" + t + \")\");\n    }\n    throw new AssertionError(msg + \" (nothing thrown)\");\n  }\n\n  static void pass(String name) { passed++; System.out.println(\"PASS: \" + name); }\n\n  static SocialNetwork net(MutableClock clock) { return new SocialNetwork(clock, new ChronologicalRanker()); }\n\n  static void befriend(SocialNetwork n, User a, User b) {\n    FriendRequest r = n.friendships().send(a.getId(), b.getId());\n    n.friendships().accept(r, b.getId());\n  }\n\n  static <T> void runAll(int threads, List<Callable<T>> jobs) throws Exception {\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(threads);\n    CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    List<Future<T>> fs = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (Callable<T> j : jobs) fs.add(pool.submit(() -> { go.await(); return j.call(); }));\n    go.countDown();\n    for (Future<T> f : fs) f.get();\n    pool.shutdown();\n  }\n\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    MutableClock clock = new MutableClock(Instant.parse(\"2026-03-02T08:00:00Z\"));\n\n    SocialNetwork n1 = net(clock);\n    User a = n1.register(\"A\"), b = n1.register(\"B\");\n    FriendRequest r = n1.friendships().send(a.getId(), b.getId());\n    check(!a.isFriendsWith(b.getId()), \"not friends before acceptance\");\n    n1.friendships().accept(r, b.getId());\n    check(a.isFriendsWith(b.getId()) && b.isFriendsWith(a.getId()), \"friendship is mutual\");\n    pass(\"accepting a request creates a mutual friendship\");\n\n    SocialNetwork n2 = net(clock);\n    User x = n2.register(\"X\"), y = n2.register(\"Y\"), z = n2.register(\"Z\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> n2.friendships().send(x.getId(), x.getId()), \"self request\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> n2.friendships().send(x.getId(), \"nope\"), \"unknown user\");\n    FriendRequest xy = n2.friendships().send(x.getId(), y.getId());\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> n2.friendships().send(y.getId(), x.getId()), \"reverse duplicate while pending\");\n    expect(SecurityException.class, () -> n2.friendships().accept(xy, x.getId()), \"sender cannot accept\");\n    n2.friendships().decline(xy, y.getId());\n    check(!x.isFriendsWith(y.getId()), \"declined request makes no friendship\");\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> n2.friendships().accept(xy, y.getId()), \"cannot accept after decline\");\n    n2.friendships().send(x.getId(), y.getId());                 // can ask again after a decline\n    check(n2.friendships().pendingFor(y.getId()).size() == 1, \"new request is pending\");\n    pass(\"friend request validation: self, unknown, duplicate, wrong actor, decline\");\n\n    SocialNetwork n3 = net(clock);\n    User p = n3.register(\"P\"), q = n3.register(\"Q\");\n    FriendRequest pq = n3.friendships().send(p.getId(), q.getId());\n    AtomicInteger accepted = new AtomicInteger();\n    List<Callable<Void>> jobs = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < 20; i++) jobs.add(() -> {\n      try { n3.friendships().accept(pq, q.getId()); accepted.incrementAndGet(); } catch (IllegalStateException ignored) { }\n      return null;\n    });\n    runAll(8, jobs);\n    check(accepted.get() == 1, \"exactly one accept wins, got \" + accepted.get());\n    pass(\"a request can be accepted only once, even concurrently\");\n\n    SocialNetwork n4 = net(clock);\n    User m = n4.register(\"M\"), k = n4.register(\"K\");\n    AtomicInteger sent = new AtomicInteger();\n    List<Callable<Void>> sends = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n      final boolean forward = i % 2 == 0;\n      sends.add(() -> {\n        try {\n          n4.friendships().send(forward ? m.getId() : k.getId(), forward ? k.getId() : m.getId());\n          sent.incrementAndGet();\n        } catch (IllegalStateException ignored) { }\n        return null;\n      });\n    }\n    runAll(8, sends);\n    check(sent.get() == 1, \"only one request between two users may be pending, got \" + sent.get());\n    pass(\"crossing friend requests: only one is created\");\n\n    SocialNetwork n5 = net(clock);\n    User au = n5.register(\"Author\"), fr = n5.register(\"Friend\"), st = n5.register(\"Stranger\");\n    befriend(n5, au, fr);\n    Post pub = n5.post(au, \"public\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    Post priv = n5.post(au, \"private\", Visibility.FRIENDS_ONLY);\n    check(pub.isVisibleTo(st) && pub.isVisibleTo(fr), \"public visible to all\");\n    check(priv.isVisibleTo(fr) && priv.isVisibleTo(au) && !priv.isVisibleTo(st), \"friends-only visible to author and friends only\");\n    expect(SecurityException.class, () -> n5.comment(st, priv, \"hi\"), \"stranger cannot comment on friends-only\");\n    expect(SecurityException.class, () -> n5.react(st, priv, ReactionType.LIKE), \"stranger cannot react to friends-only\");\n    n5.comment(st, pub, \"fine\");\n    pass(\"visibility rules are enforced for reading, commenting and reacting\");\n\n    n5.react(fr, pub, ReactionType.LIKE);\n    n5.react(fr, pub, ReactionType.LOVE);\n    check(pub.reactionCount() == 1 && pub.reactionBreakdown().get(ReactionType.LOVE) == 1, \"second reaction replaces the first\");\n    n5.unreact(fr, pub);\n    check(pub.reactionCount() == 0, \"reaction removed\");\n    pass(\"one reaction per user per post; changing replaces, removing clears\");\n\n    Comment c1 = n5.comment(fr, pub, \"top\");\n    Comment c2 = n5.reply(au, pub, c1, \"reply\");\n    n5.reply(fr, pub, c2, \"reply to reply\");\n    check(c1.totalCount() == 3, \"thread of three\");\n    check(pub.commentCount() == 4, \"four comments including the stranger's: \" + pub.commentCount());\n    pass(\"nested comments are counted as a tree\");\n\n    SocialNetwork n6 = net(clock);\n    User hub = n6.register(\"Hub\");\n    Post busy = n6.post(hub, \"busy\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    List<Callable<Void>> work = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < 300; i++) {\n      User u = n6.register(\"u\" + i);\n      work.add(() -> { n6.react(u, busy, ReactionType.LIKE); n6.comment(u, busy, \"c\"); return null; });\n    }\n    User same = n6.register(\"same\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n      ReactionType t = ReactionType.values()[i % 3];\n      work.add(() -> { n6.react(same, busy, t); return null; });\n    }\n    runAll(16, work);\n    check(busy.reactionCount() == 301, \"300 distinct reactors plus one user, got \" + busy.reactionCount());\n    check(busy.commentCount() == 300, \"no lost comments, got \" + busy.commentCount());\n    pass(\"no lost reactions or comments under 400 concurrent operations\");\n\n    MutableClock c = new MutableClock(Instant.parse(\"2026-03-02T08:00:00Z\"));\n    SocialNetwork n7 = net(c);\n    User v = n7.register(\"Viewer\"), f1 = n7.register(\"F1\"), f2 = n7.register(\"F2\"), st2 = n7.register(\"S\");\n    befriend(n7, v, f1);\n    befriend(n7, v, f2);\n    Post old = n7.post(f1, \"old but loved\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    c.advance(Duration.ofHours(5));\n    Post fresh = n7.post(f2, \"fresh\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    n7.post(f1, \"hidden\", Visibility.FRIENDS_ONLY);                  // visible: f1 is a friend of v\n    n7.post(st2, \"stranger\", Visibility.PUBLIC);                     // not a friend: never in the feed\n    n7.post(f2, \"mine to share\", Visibility.FRIENDS_ONLY);\n    List<Post> chrono = n7.feed().feedFor(v.getId(), 10);\n    check(chrono.size() == 4, \"feed holds friends' posts only: \" + chrono.size());\n    check(chrono.get(chrono.size() - 1) == old, \"oldest post last in chronological order\");\n    check(n7.feed().feedFor(v.getId(), 2).size() == 2, \"limit respected\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 20; i++) n7.react(n7.register(\"r\" + i), old, ReactionType.LIKE);\n    n7.feed().setRanker(new EngagementRanker(c));\n    check(n7.feed().feedFor(v.getId(), 10).get(0) == old, \"engagement ranking lifts the loved post to the top\");\n    check(n7.feed().feedFor(st2.getId(), 10).isEmpty(), \"a user with no friends has an empty feed\");\n    pass(\"feed shows friends' visible posts; ranker swapped at runtime\");\n\n    SocialNetwork n8 = net(clock);\n    InAppSubscriber inbox = new InAppSubscriber(n8.users());\n    n8.notifications().subscribe(inbox);\n    User o = n8.register(\"Owner\"), g = n8.register(\"Guest\");\n    Post op = n8.post(o, \"p\", Visibility.PUBLIC);\n    n8.react(o, op, ReactionType.LIKE);\n    n8.comment(o, op, \"self comment\");\n    check(inbox.inbox(o.getId()).isEmpty(), \"no self-notifications\");\n    n8.react(g, op, ReactionType.LIKE);\n    n8.react(g, op, ReactionType.LIKE);                              // unchanged reaction: no second notice\n    n8.comment(g, op, \"nice\");\n    check(inbox.inbox(o.getId()).size() == 2, \"one reaction notice and one comment notice: \" + inbox.inbox(o.getId()));\n    List<String> extra = new ArrayList<>();\n    n8.notifications().subscribe(e -> extra.add(e.type().name()));\n    n8.notifications().subscribe(e -> { throw new IllegalStateException(\"broken channel\"); });\n    n8.comment(g, op, \"again\");\n    check(extra.equals(List.of(\"COMMENT\")), \"new subscriber receives events: \" + extra);\n    check(op.commentCount() == 3, \"a failing subscriber does not stop the comment\");\n    pass(\"notifications: no self-notices, de-duplicated, extensible, failure-isolated\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"All \" + passed + \" tests passed\");\n  }\n}","output":"PASS: accepting a request creates a mutual friendship\nPASS: friend request validation: self, unknown, duplicate, wrong actor, decline\nPASS: a request can be accepted only once, even concurrently\nPASS: crossing friend requests: only one is created\nPASS: visibility rules are enforced for reading, commenting and reacting\nPASS: one reaction per user per post; changing replaces, removing clears\nPASS: nested comments are counted as a tree\nPASS: no lost reactions or comments under 400 concurrent operations\nPASS: feed shows friends' visible posts; ranker swapped at runtime\nPASS: notifications: no self-notices, de-duplicated, extensible, failure-isolated\nAll 10 tests passed"},"complexity":["Friend check: O(1) with a hash set.","React or unreact: O(1).","Comment count: O(n) in the size of the comment tree.","Feed: O(F x P) to gather the posts of F friends with P posts each, plus O(n log n) to rank n candidates."]});
window.SOLUTIONS.push({"id":"restaurant-management-system","intro":"The floor, the kitchen and the till connect through three small mechanisms: a table service that hands out tables safely, an order with a controlled lifecycle that announces its changes to listeners, and a billing service whose discounts are strategies. `RestaurantService` is the facade a waiter uses. Every file compiles with plain `javac`; the demo output and test results below are from a real run.","steps":[{"title":"Requirement 1: seating guests safely","text":"`TableService` is the only place that changes a table's status. Finding a free table and marking it occupied happen inside one `synchronized` method, so two waiters cannot both see Table 4 as free and seat two parties there. Choosing the smallest table that fits keeps large tables for large parties. Reservations later reuse the same search and just end with `RESERVED` instead of `OCCUPIED`, so the model already has room for them.","code":[{"file":"Table.java","body":"public class Table {\n  public enum Status { AVAILABLE, OCCUPIED, RESERVED }\n\n  private final int id;\n  private final int capacity;\n  private Status status = Status.AVAILABLE;   // only TableService changes this, under its lock\n\n  public Table(int id, int capacity) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.capacity = capacity;\n  }\n\n  public int id() { return id; }\n  public int capacity() { return capacity; }\n  Status status() { return status; }\n  void setStatus(Status status) { this.status = status; }\n\n  @Override public String toString() { return \"Table \" + id + \" (seats \" + capacity + \")\"; }\n}"},{"file":"NoTableAvailableException.java","body":"public class NoTableAvailableException extends RuntimeException {\n  public NoTableAvailableException(int partySize) {\n    super(\"No free table for a party of \" + partySize);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"TableService.java","body":"import java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\npublic class TableService {\n  private final List<Table> tables;\n\n  public TableService(List<Table> tables) {\n    this.tables = tables;\n  }\n\n  // Find and claim in one critical section so two waiters cannot get the same table.\n  public synchronized Optional<Table> seat(int partySize) {\n    return claim(partySize, Table.Status.OCCUPIED);\n  }\n\n  // Reservations reuse the same search; the table just ends up RESERVED instead of OCCUPIED.\n  public synchronized Optional<Table> reserve(int partySize) {\n    return claim(partySize, Table.Status.RESERVED);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized void seatReserved(Table table) {\n    if (table.status() != Table.Status.RESERVED)\n      throw new IllegalStateException(table + \" is not reserved\");\n    table.setStatus(Table.Status.OCCUPIED);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized void free(Table table) {\n    if (table.status() == Table.Status.AVAILABLE)\n      throw new IllegalStateException(table + \" is already free\");\n    table.setStatus(Table.Status.AVAILABLE);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized long availableCount() {\n    return tables.stream().filter(t -> t.status() == Table.Status.AVAILABLE).count();\n  }\n\n  private Optional<Table> claim(int partySize, Table.Status next) {\n    if (partySize <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Party size must be positive\");\n    Optional<Table> best = tables.stream()\n        .filter(t -> t.status() == Table.Status.AVAILABLE && t.capacity() >= partySize)\n        .min(Comparator.comparingInt(Table::capacity));   // smallest table that fits\n    best.ifPresent(t -> t.setStatus(next));\n    return best;\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 2: orders hold a price snapshot","text":"`OrderItem` copies the item's name and price at the moment of ordering. If the menu price changes during the meal, the bill still charges what the guest was shown. A `Visit` collects every order of one party's stay, and refuses new orders once the visit has been paid.","code":[{"file":"MenuItem.java","body":"public class MenuItem {\n  private final String name;\n  private final long priceCents;\n\n  public MenuItem(String name, long priceCents) {\n    this.name = name;\n    this.priceCents = priceCents;\n  }\n\n  public String name() { return name; }\n  public long priceCents() { return priceCents; }\n}"},{"file":"Menu.java","body":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\npublic class Menu {\n  private final Map<String, MenuItem> items = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n  public void add(String name, long priceCents) { items.put(name, new MenuItem(name, priceCents)); }\n\n  public MenuItem find(String name) {\n    MenuItem item = items.get(name);\n    if (item == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Not on the menu: \" + name);\n    return item;\n  }\n\n  // The kitchen can change a price at any time; orders already placed keep the old one.\n  public void reprice(String name, long newPriceCents) { add(name, newPriceCents); }\n}"},{"file":"OrderItem.java","body":"public final class OrderItem {\n  private final String name;\n  private final long unitPriceCents;\n  private final int quantity;\n\n  public OrderItem(MenuItem item, int quantity) {\n    if (quantity <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Quantity must be positive\");\n    this.name = item.name();\n    this.unitPriceCents = item.priceCents(); // snapshot, not a live reference\n    this.quantity = quantity;\n  }\n\n  public long totalCents() { return unitPriceCents * quantity; }\n  public String name() { return name; }\n  public int quantity() { return quantity; }\n}"},{"file":"Visit.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// One party at one table, from being seated until they pay.\npublic class Visit {\n  private final Table table;\n  private final int partySize;\n  private final List<Order> orders = new ArrayList<>();\n  private boolean closed;\n\n  public Visit(Table table, int partySize) {\n    this.table = table;\n    this.partySize = partySize;\n  }\n\n  synchronized void addOrder(Order o) {\n    if (closed) throw new IllegalStateException(\"This visit is already paid and closed\");\n    orders.add(o);\n  }\n\n  synchronized void close() { closed = true; }\n  synchronized boolean isClosed() { return closed; }\n  public synchronized List<Order> orders() { return new ArrayList<>(orders); }\n  public Table table() { return table; }\n  public int partySize() { return partySize; }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 3: a controlled order lifecycle","text":"An order moves only through legal steps, and the allowed transitions sit next to the statuses in `canMoveTo`. `Order.advance` is the only way to change status and it is synchronized, so when two threads try the same move exactly one wins. A served order can never go back to preparing, and an order can be cancelled only before the kitchen starts it.","code":[{"file":"OrderStatus.java","body":"public enum OrderStatus {\n  PLACED, PREPARING, READY, SERVED, CANCELLED;\n\n  public boolean canMoveTo(OrderStatus next) {\n    switch (this) {\n      case PLACED:    return next == PREPARING || next == CANCELLED;\n      case PREPARING: return next == READY;\n      case READY:     return next == SERVED;\n      default:        return false; // SERVED and CANCELLED are terminal\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"Order.java  ›  advance","body":"public void advance(OrderStatus next) {\n  OrderStatus previous;\n  synchronized (this) {\n    if (!status.canMoveTo(next)) {\n      throw new IllegalStateException(\"Cannot move order \" + id + \" from \" + status + \" to \" + next);\n    }\n    previous = status;\n    status = next;\n  }\n  for (OrderListener listener : listeners) {     // notify outside the lock\n    listener.onStatusChanged(this, previous, next);\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 4: the kitchen and waiters listen, the order does not know them","text":"Consumers register as `OrderListener`s and the order calls them without knowing who they are. Adding an SMS to the guest later is one more listener. Listeners are notified after the lock is released. Orders are created without announcing themselves; `announcePlaced` is called only after the visit has accepted the order, so the kitchen never receives a ticket for an order that was rejected.","code":[{"file":"OrderListener.java","body":"public interface OrderListener {\n  // `from` is null for the very first event, when the order is placed.\n  void onStatusChanged(Order order, OrderStatus from, OrderStatus to);\n}"},{"file":"Order.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class Order {\n  private final long id;\n  private final Table table;\n  private final List<OrderItem> items;\n  private OrderStatus status = OrderStatus.PLACED;\n  private final List<OrderListener> listeners = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  private Order(long id, Table table, List<OrderItem> items) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.table = table;\n    this.items = List.copyOf(items);\n  }\n\n  // Builds the order and registers the listeners, but tells nobody yet.\n  public static Order create(long id, Table table, List<OrderItem> items, List<OrderListener> listeners) {\n    if (items.isEmpty()) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"An order needs at least one item\");\n    Order order = new Order(id, table, items);\n    order.listeners.addAll(listeners);\n    return order;\n  }\n\n  // Called only once the order has been accepted, so the kitchen never sees a rejected order.\n  public void announcePlaced() {\n    for (OrderListener l : listeners) l.onStatusChanged(this, null, OrderStatus.PLACED);\n  }\n\n  public void advance(OrderStatus next) {\n    OrderStatus previous;\n    synchronized (this) {\n      if (!status.canMoveTo(next)) {\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"Cannot move order \" + id + \" from \" + status + \" to \" + next);\n      }\n      previous = status;\n      status = next;\n    }\n    for (OrderListener listener : listeners) {     // notify outside the lock\n      listener.onStatusChanged(this, previous, next);\n    }\n  }\n\n  public long id() { return id; }\n  public Table table() { return table; }\n  public List<OrderItem> items() { return items; }\n  public synchronized OrderStatus status() { return status; }\n\n  public long subtotalCents() {\n    return items.stream().mapToLong(OrderItem::totalCents).sum();\n  }\n}"},{"file":"KitchenDisplay.java","body":"public class KitchenDisplay implements OrderListener {\n  public void onStatusChanged(Order order, OrderStatus from, OrderStatus to) {\n    if (to == OrderStatus.PLACED) {\n      StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n      for (OrderItem i : order.items()) sb.append(i.quantity()).append(\"x \").append(i.name()).append(\"  \");\n      System.out.println(\"  [KITCHEN] New order \" + order.id() + \" for table \" + order.table().id() + \": \" + sb.toString().trim());\n    } else if (to == OrderStatus.CANCELLED) {\n      System.out.println(\"  [KITCHEN] Order \" + order.id() + \" cancelled, stop prep\");\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"WaiterPager.java","body":"public class WaiterPager implements OrderListener {\n  public void onStatusChanged(Order order, OrderStatus from, OrderStatus to) {\n    if (to == OrderStatus.READY) {\n      System.out.println(\"  [PAGER] Order \" + order.id() + \" is ready for table \" + order.table().id());\n    }\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 5: billing with pluggable discounts","text":"The bill adds up every order of the visit, skips cancelled ones, applies one discount and then adds tax on what the guest actually pays. The discount is a `DiscountStrategy`, so a festival offer or a manager override is a new class that `BillingService` never sees. `BestOf` shows strategies composing: it gives the guest whichever offer saves the most.","code":[{"file":"DiscountStrategy.java","body":"public interface DiscountStrategy {\n  long discountFor(long subtotalCents);\n}"},{"file":"NoDiscount.java","body":"public class NoDiscount implements DiscountStrategy {\n  public long discountFor(long subtotalCents) { return 0; }\n}"},{"file":"PercentOff.java","body":"public class PercentOff implements DiscountStrategy {\n  private final int percent;\n\n  public PercentOff(int percent) { this.percent = percent; }\n\n  public long discountFor(long subtotalCents) {\n    return subtotalCents * percent / 100;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"FlatOff.java","body":"public class FlatOff implements DiscountStrategy {\n  private final long cents;\n\n  public FlatOff(long cents) { this.cents = cents; }\n\n  public long discountFor(long subtotalCents) { return cents; }\n}"},{"file":"BestOf.java","body":"// Gives the guest whichever offer saves the most. Strategies compose.\npublic class BestOf implements DiscountStrategy {\n  private final DiscountStrategy[] options;\n\n  public BestOf(DiscountStrategy... options) { this.options = options; }\n\n  public long discountFor(long subtotalCents) {\n    long best = 0;\n    for (DiscountStrategy d : options) best = Math.max(best, d.discountFor(subtotalCents));\n    return best;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"Bill.java","body":"public final class Bill {\n  public final long subtotalCents;\n  public final long discountCents;\n  public final long taxCents;\n  public final long totalCents;\n\n  public Bill(long subtotalCents, long discountCents, long taxCents, long totalCents) {\n    this.subtotalCents = subtotalCents;\n    this.discountCents = discountCents;\n    this.taxCents = taxCents;\n    this.totalCents = totalCents;\n  }\n\n  public static String fmt(long cents) { return String.format(\"$%d.%02d\", cents / 100, cents % 100); }\n\n  @Override public String toString() {\n    return \"  Subtotal  \" + fmt(subtotalCents) + \"\\n\"\n         + \"  Discount -\" + fmt(discountCents) + \"\\n\"\n         + \"  Tax (5%)  \" + fmt(taxCents) + \"\\n\"\n         + \"  TOTAL     \" + fmt(totalCents);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"BillingService.java","body":"import java.util.List;\n\npublic class BillingService {\n  private static final int TAX_PERCENT = 5;\n\n  // Discount first, then tax on what the guest actually pays. Tax rounds down to the cent.\n  public Bill billFor(List<Order> orders, DiscountStrategy discount) {\n    long subtotal = orders.stream()\n        .filter(o -> o.status() != OrderStatus.CANCELLED)\n        .mapToLong(Order::subtotalCents)\n        .sum();\n    long discountAmount = Math.min(subtotal, discount.discountFor(subtotal));\n    long taxable = subtotal - discountAmount;\n    long tax = taxable * TAX_PERCENT / 100;\n    return new Bill(subtotal, discountAmount, tax, taxable + tax);\n  }\n}"}]},{"title":"The facade","text":"`RestaurantService` is what a waiter calls: seat a party, place an order, check out. `checkout` refuses to bill while an order is still in progress, then closes the visit and frees the table.","code":[{"file":"RestaurantService.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\n// Facade used by waiters: seat, order, advance, pay.\npublic class RestaurantService {\n  private final TableService tables;\n  private final Menu menu;\n  private final BillingService billing = new BillingService();\n  private final List<OrderListener> listeners = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n  private final AtomicLong orderIds = new AtomicLong();\n\n  public RestaurantService(TableService tables, Menu menu) {\n    this.tables = tables;\n    this.menu = menu;\n  }\n\n  public void addListener(OrderListener l) { listeners.add(l); }\n\n  public Visit seatParty(int partySize) {\n    Table t = tables.seat(partySize).orElseThrow(() -> new NoTableAvailableException(partySize));\n    return new Visit(t, partySize);\n  }\n\n  public Order placeOrder(Visit visit, Map<String, Integer> lines) {\n    List<OrderItem> items = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> e : lines.entrySet())\n      items.add(new OrderItem(menu.find(e.getKey()), e.getValue()));   // price captured here\n    Order order = Order.create(orderIds.incrementAndGet(), visit.table(), items, listeners);\n    visit.addOrder(order);            // rejects the order if the visit is already closed\n    order.announcePlaced();           // only now does the kitchen hear about it\n    return order;\n  }\n\n  public Bill checkout(Visit visit, DiscountStrategy discount) {\n    List<Order> orders = visit.orders();\n    for (Order o : orders) {\n      OrderStatus s = o.status();\n      if (s != OrderStatus.SERVED && s != OrderStatus.CANCELLED)\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"Order \" + o.id() + \" is still \" + s);\n    }\n    Bill bill = billing.billFor(orders, discount);\n    visit.close();\n    tables.free(visit.table());\n    return bill;\n  }\n}"}]}],"files":[{"file":"Table.java","body":"public class Table {\n  public enum Status { AVAILABLE, OCCUPIED, RESERVED }\n\n  private final int id;\n  private final int capacity;\n  private Status status = Status.AVAILABLE;   // only TableService changes this, under its lock\n\n  public Table(int id, int capacity) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.capacity = capacity;\n  }\n\n  public int id() { return id; }\n  public int capacity() { return capacity; }\n  Status status() { return status; }\n  void setStatus(Status status) { this.status = status; }\n\n  @Override public String toString() { return \"Table \" + id + \" (seats \" + capacity + \")\"; }\n}"},{"file":"NoTableAvailableException.java","body":"public class NoTableAvailableException extends RuntimeException {\n  public NoTableAvailableException(int partySize) {\n    super(\"No free table for a party of \" + partySize);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"TableService.java","body":"import java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\npublic class TableService {\n  private final List<Table> tables;\n\n  public TableService(List<Table> tables) {\n    this.tables = tables;\n  }\n\n  // Find and claim in one critical section so two waiters cannot get the same table.\n  public synchronized Optional<Table> seat(int partySize) {\n    return claim(partySize, Table.Status.OCCUPIED);\n  }\n\n  // Reservations reuse the same search; the table just ends up RESERVED instead of OCCUPIED.\n  public synchronized Optional<Table> reserve(int partySize) {\n    return claim(partySize, Table.Status.RESERVED);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized void seatReserved(Table table) {\n    if (table.status() != Table.Status.RESERVED)\n      throw new IllegalStateException(table + \" is not reserved\");\n    table.setStatus(Table.Status.OCCUPIED);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized void free(Table table) {\n    if (table.status() == Table.Status.AVAILABLE)\n      throw new IllegalStateException(table + \" is already free\");\n    table.setStatus(Table.Status.AVAILABLE);\n  }\n\n  public synchronized long availableCount() {\n    return tables.stream().filter(t -> t.status() == Table.Status.AVAILABLE).count();\n  }\n\n  private Optional<Table> claim(int partySize, Table.Status next) {\n    if (partySize <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Party size must be positive\");\n    Optional<Table> best = tables.stream()\n        .filter(t -> t.status() == Table.Status.AVAILABLE && t.capacity() >= partySize)\n        .min(Comparator.comparingInt(Table::capacity));   // smallest table that fits\n    best.ifPresent(t -> t.setStatus(next));\n    return best;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"MenuItem.java","body":"public class MenuItem {\n  private final String name;\n  private final long priceCents;\n\n  public MenuItem(String name, long priceCents) {\n    this.name = name;\n    this.priceCents = priceCents;\n  }\n\n  public String name() { return name; }\n  public long priceCents() { return priceCents; }\n}"},{"file":"Menu.java","body":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\npublic class Menu {\n  private final Map<String, MenuItem> items = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n  public void add(String name, long priceCents) { items.put(name, new MenuItem(name, priceCents)); }\n\n  public MenuItem find(String name) {\n    MenuItem item = items.get(name);\n    if (item == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Not on the menu: \" + name);\n    return item;\n  }\n\n  // The kitchen can change a price at any time; orders already placed keep the old one.\n  public void reprice(String name, long newPriceCents) { add(name, newPriceCents); }\n}"},{"file":"OrderItem.java","body":"public final class OrderItem {\n  private final String name;\n  private final long unitPriceCents;\n  private final int quantity;\n\n  public OrderItem(MenuItem item, int quantity) {\n    if (quantity <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Quantity must be positive\");\n    this.name = item.name();\n    this.unitPriceCents = item.priceCents(); // snapshot, not a live reference\n    this.quantity = quantity;\n  }\n\n  public long totalCents() { return unitPriceCents * quantity; }\n  public String name() { return name; }\n  public int quantity() { return quantity; }\n}"},{"file":"OrderStatus.java","body":"public enum OrderStatus {\n  PLACED, PREPARING, READY, SERVED, CANCELLED;\n\n  public boolean canMoveTo(OrderStatus next) {\n    switch (this) {\n      case PLACED:    return next == PREPARING || next == CANCELLED;\n      case PREPARING: return next == READY;\n      case READY:     return next == SERVED;\n      default:        return false; // SERVED and CANCELLED are terminal\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"OrderListener.java","body":"public interface OrderListener {\n  // `from` is null for the very first event, when the order is placed.\n  void onStatusChanged(Order order, OrderStatus from, OrderStatus to);\n}"},{"file":"Order.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class Order {\n  private final long id;\n  private final Table table;\n  private final List<OrderItem> items;\n  private OrderStatus status = OrderStatus.PLACED;\n  private final List<OrderListener> listeners = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  private Order(long id, Table table, List<OrderItem> items) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.table = table;\n    this.items = List.copyOf(items);\n  }\n\n  // Builds the order and registers the listeners, but tells nobody yet.\n  public static Order create(long id, Table table, List<OrderItem> items, List<OrderListener> listeners) {\n    if (items.isEmpty()) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"An order needs at least one item\");\n    Order order = new Order(id, table, items);\n    order.listeners.addAll(listeners);\n    return order;\n  }\n\n  // Called only once the order has been accepted, so the kitchen never sees a rejected order.\n  public void announcePlaced() {\n    for (OrderListener l : listeners) l.onStatusChanged(this, null, OrderStatus.PLACED);\n  }\n\n  public void advance(OrderStatus next) {\n    OrderStatus previous;\n    synchronized (this) {\n      if (!status.canMoveTo(next)) {\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"Cannot move order \" + id + \" from \" + status + \" to \" + next);\n      }\n      previous = status;\n      status = next;\n    }\n    for (OrderListener listener : listeners) {     // notify outside the lock\n      listener.onStatusChanged(this, previous, next);\n    }\n  }\n\n  public long id() { return id; }\n  public Table table() { return table; }\n  public List<OrderItem> items() { return items; }\n  public synchronized OrderStatus status() { return status; }\n\n  public long subtotalCents() {\n    return items.stream().mapToLong(OrderItem::totalCents).sum();\n  }\n}"},{"file":"KitchenDisplay.java","body":"public class KitchenDisplay implements OrderListener {\n  public void onStatusChanged(Order order, OrderStatus from, OrderStatus to) {\n    if (to == OrderStatus.PLACED) {\n      StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n      for (OrderItem i : order.items()) sb.append(i.quantity()).append(\"x \").append(i.name()).append(\"  \");\n      System.out.println(\"  [KITCHEN] New order \" + order.id() + \" for table \" + order.table().id() + \": \" + sb.toString().trim());\n    } else if (to == OrderStatus.CANCELLED) {\n      System.out.println(\"  [KITCHEN] Order \" + order.id() + \" cancelled, stop prep\");\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"WaiterPager.java","body":"public class WaiterPager implements OrderListener {\n  public void onStatusChanged(Order order, OrderStatus from, OrderStatus to) {\n    if (to == OrderStatus.READY) {\n      System.out.println(\"  [PAGER] Order \" + order.id() + \" is ready for table \" + order.table().id());\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"file":"DiscountStrategy.java","body":"public interface DiscountStrategy {\n  long discountFor(long subtotalCents);\n}"},{"file":"NoDiscount.java","body":"public class NoDiscount implements DiscountStrategy {\n  public long discountFor(long subtotalCents) { return 0; }\n}"},{"file":"PercentOff.java","body":"public class PercentOff implements DiscountStrategy {\n  private final int percent;\n\n  public PercentOff(int percent) { this.percent = percent; }\n\n  public long discountFor(long subtotalCents) {\n    return subtotalCents * percent / 100;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"FlatOff.java","body":"public class FlatOff implements DiscountStrategy {\n  private final long cents;\n\n  public FlatOff(long cents) { this.cents = cents; }\n\n  public long discountFor(long subtotalCents) { return cents; }\n}"},{"file":"BestOf.java","body":"// Gives the guest whichever offer saves the most. Strategies compose.\npublic class BestOf implements DiscountStrategy {\n  private final DiscountStrategy[] options;\n\n  public BestOf(DiscountStrategy... options) { this.options = options; }\n\n  public long discountFor(long subtotalCents) {\n    long best = 0;\n    for (DiscountStrategy d : options) best = Math.max(best, d.discountFor(subtotalCents));\n    return best;\n  }\n}"},{"file":"Bill.java","body":"public final class Bill {\n  public final long subtotalCents;\n  public final long discountCents;\n  public final long taxCents;\n  public final long totalCents;\n\n  public Bill(long subtotalCents, long discountCents, long taxCents, long totalCents) {\n    this.subtotalCents = subtotalCents;\n    this.discountCents = discountCents;\n    this.taxCents = taxCents;\n    this.totalCents = totalCents;\n  }\n\n  public static String fmt(long cents) { return String.format(\"$%d.%02d\", cents / 100, cents % 100); }\n\n  @Override public String toString() {\n    return \"  Subtotal  \" + fmt(subtotalCents) + \"\\n\"\n         + \"  Discount -\" + fmt(discountCents) + \"\\n\"\n         + \"  Tax (5%)  \" + fmt(taxCents) + \"\\n\"\n         + \"  TOTAL     \" + fmt(totalCents);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"BillingService.java","body":"import java.util.List;\n\npublic class BillingService {\n  private static final int TAX_PERCENT = 5;\n\n  // Discount first, then tax on what the guest actually pays. Tax rounds down to the cent.\n  public Bill billFor(List<Order> orders, DiscountStrategy discount) {\n    long subtotal = orders.stream()\n        .filter(o -> o.status() != OrderStatus.CANCELLED)\n        .mapToLong(Order::subtotalCents)\n        .sum();\n    long discountAmount = Math.min(subtotal, discount.discountFor(subtotal));\n    long taxable = subtotal - discountAmount;\n    long tax = taxable * TAX_PERCENT / 100;\n    return new Bill(subtotal, discountAmount, tax, taxable + tax);\n  }\n}"},{"file":"Visit.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// One party at one table, from being seated until they pay.\npublic class Visit {\n  private final Table table;\n  private final int partySize;\n  private final List<Order> orders = new ArrayList<>();\n  private boolean closed;\n\n  public Visit(Table table, int partySize) {\n    this.table = table;\n    this.partySize = partySize;\n  }\n\n  synchronized void addOrder(Order o) {\n    if (closed) throw new IllegalStateException(\"This visit is already paid and closed\");\n    orders.add(o);\n  }\n\n  synchronized void close() { closed = true; }\n  synchronized boolean isClosed() { return closed; }\n  public synchronized List<Order> orders() { return new ArrayList<>(orders); }\n  public Table table() { return table; }\n  public int partySize() { return partySize; }\n}"},{"file":"RestaurantService.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\n// Facade used by waiters: seat, order, advance, pay.\npublic class RestaurantService {\n  private final TableService tables;\n  private final Menu menu;\n  private final BillingService billing = new BillingService();\n  private final List<OrderListener> listeners = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n  private final AtomicLong orderIds = new AtomicLong();\n\n  public RestaurantService(TableService tables, Menu menu) {\n    this.tables = tables;\n    this.menu = menu;\n  }\n\n  public void addListener(OrderListener l) { listeners.add(l); }\n\n  public Visit seatParty(int partySize) {\n    Table t = tables.seat(partySize).orElseThrow(() -> new NoTableAvailableException(partySize));\n    return new Visit(t, partySize);\n  }\n\n  public Order placeOrder(Visit visit, Map<String, Integer> lines) {\n    List<OrderItem> items = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> e : lines.entrySet())\n      items.add(new OrderItem(menu.find(e.getKey()), e.getValue()));   // price captured here\n    Order order = Order.create(orderIds.incrementAndGet(), visit.table(), items, listeners);\n    visit.addOrder(order);            // rejects the order if the visit is already closed\n    order.announcePlaced();           // only now does the kitchen hear about it\n    return order;\n  }\n\n  public Bill checkout(Visit visit, DiscountStrategy discount) {\n    List<Order> orders = visit.orders();\n    for (Order o : orders) {\n      OrderStatus s = o.status();\n      if (s != OrderStatus.SERVED && s != OrderStatus.CANCELLED)\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"Order \" + o.id() + \" is still \" + s);\n    }\n    Bill bill = billing.billFor(orders, discount);\n    visit.close();\n    tables.free(visit.table());\n    return bill;\n  }\n}"}],"driver":{"text":"The demo seats parties, places and cancels orders, shows the lifecycle rejecting illegal jumps, proves that a menu price change does not touch an open order, bills with the best of two discounts, reserves a table, and races 50 waiters for one table.","file":"Main.java","body":"import java.util.LinkedHashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    TableService tables = new TableService(List.of(\n        new Table(1, 2), new Table(2, 2), new Table(3, 4), new Table(4, 6)));\n    Menu menu = new Menu();\n    menu.add(\"Pasta\", 1200);\n    menu.add(\"Cola\", 250);\n    menu.add(\"Tiramisu\", 700);\n    RestaurantService restaurant = new RestaurantService(tables, menu);\n    restaurant.addListener(new KitchenDisplay());\n    restaurant.addListener(new WaiterPager());\n\n    System.out.println(\"== 1. Seating: smallest table that fits ==\");\n    Visit party3 = restaurant.seatParty(3);\n    System.out.println(\"Party of 3 -> \" + party3.table());\n    Visit party2 = restaurant.seatParty(2);\n    System.out.println(\"Party of 2 -> \" + party2.table());\n    try {\n      restaurant.seatParty(7);\n    } catch (NoTableAvailableException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Party of 7 -> \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 2. Orders (a table can order more than once) ==\");\n    Order o1 = restaurant.placeOrder(party3, items(\"Pasta\", 2, \"Cola\", 3));\n    Order o2 = restaurant.placeOrder(party3, items(\"Tiramisu\", 1));\n    System.out.println(\"Orders for table \" + party3.table().id() + \": \" + party3.orders().size());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 3. Order lifecycle ==\");\n    try {\n      o1.advance(OrderStatus.SERVED);\n    } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Rejected: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n    o1.advance(OrderStatus.PREPARING);\n    try {\n      o1.advance(OrderStatus.CANCELLED);\n    } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Rejected: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n    o1.advance(OrderStatus.READY);\n    o1.advance(OrderStatus.SERVED);\n    System.out.println(\"Order \" + o1.id() + \" is \" + o1.status());\n    o2.advance(OrderStatus.CANCELLED);\n    System.out.println(\"Order \" + o2.id() + \" is \" + o2.status());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 4. Menu price changes do not touch an open order ==\");\n    menu.reprice(\"Pasta\", 1500);\n    Order o3 = restaurant.placeOrder(party3, items(\"Pasta\", 1));\n    for (OrderStatus s : new OrderStatus[] { OrderStatus.PREPARING, OrderStatus.READY, OrderStatus.SERVED }) o3.advance(s);\n    System.out.println(\"Order \" + o1.id() + \" still costs \" + Bill.fmt(o1.subtotalCents()) + \" (2 Pasta + 3 Cola at the old price)\");\n    System.out.println(\"Order \" + o3.id() + \" costs \" + Bill.fmt(o3.subtotalCents()) + \" (1 Pasta at the new price)\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 5. Billing ==\");\n    try {\n      restaurant.placeOrder(party3, items(\"Cola\", 1));\n      restaurant.checkout(party3, new NoDiscount());\n    } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Checkout blocked: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n    party3.orders().get(party3.orders().size() - 1).advance(OrderStatus.CANCELLED);\n    DiscountStrategy offer = new BestOf(new PercentOff(10), new FlatOff(500));\n    Bill bill = restaurant.checkout(party3, offer);\n    System.out.println(\"Bill for table 3 (cancelled order excluded, best of 10% / $5.00 off):\");\n    System.out.println(bill);\n    System.out.println(\"Table 3 is free again; free tables: \" + tables.availableCount() + \" of 4\");\n    try {\n      restaurant.placeOrder(party3, items(\"Cola\", 1));\n    } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n      System.out.println(\"Ordering after paying: \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 6. Reservations use the same tables ==\");\n    Table reserved = tables.reserve(2).orElseThrow();\n    System.out.println(\"Reserved \" + reserved + \"; free tables now \" + tables.availableCount());\n    tables.seatReserved(reserved);\n    System.out.println(\"Guests arrive, \" + reserved + \" is occupied\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 7. Two waiters, one table ==\");\n    TableService one = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 4)));\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(8);\n    CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    List<Future<Boolean>> results = new java.util.ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n      results.add(pool.submit(() -> { go.await(); return one.seat(3).isPresent(); }));\n    }\n    go.countDown();\n    int seated = 0;\n    for (Future<Boolean> f : results) if (f.get()) seated++;\n    pool.shutdown();\n    System.out.println(\"50 waiters tried to seat a party at the only table: seated=\" + seated);\n  }\n\n  private static Map<String, Integer> items(Object... pairs) {\n    Map<String, Integer> m = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < pairs.length; i += 2) m.put((String) pairs[i], (Integer) pairs[i + 1]);\n    return m;\n  }\n}","output":"== 1. Seating: smallest table that fits ==\nParty of 3 -> Table 3 (seats 4)\nParty of 2 -> Table 1 (seats 2)\nParty of 7 -> No free table for a party of 7\n\n== 2. Orders (a table can order more than once) ==\n  [KITCHEN] New order 1 for table 3: 2x Pasta  3x Cola\n  [KITCHEN] New order 2 for table 3: 1x Tiramisu\nOrders for table 3: 2\n\n== 3. Order lifecycle ==\nRejected: Cannot move order 1 from PLACED to SERVED\nRejected: Cannot move order 1 from PREPARING to CANCELLED\n  [PAGER] Order 1 is ready for table 3\nOrder 1 is SERVED\n  [KITCHEN] Order 2 cancelled, stop prep\nOrder 2 is CANCELLED\n\n== 4. Menu price changes do not touch an open order ==\n  [KITCHEN] New order 3 for table 3: 1x Pasta\n  [PAGER] Order 3 is ready for table 3\nOrder 1 still costs $31.50 (2 Pasta + 3 Cola at the old price)\nOrder 3 costs $15.00 (1 Pasta at the new price)\n\n== 5. Billing ==\n  [KITCHEN] New order 4 for table 3: 1x Cola\nCheckout blocked: Order 4 is still PLACED\n  [KITCHEN] Order 4 cancelled, stop prep\nBill for table 3 (cancelled order excluded, best of 10% / $5.00 off):\n  Subtotal  $46.50\n  Discount -$5.00\n  Tax (5%)  $2.07\n  TOTAL     $43.57\nTable 3 is free again; free tables: 3 of 4\nOrdering after paying: This visit is already paid and closed\n\n== 6. Reservations use the same tables ==\nReserved Table 2 (seats 2); free tables now 2\nGuests arrive, Table 2 (seats 2) is occupied\n\n== 7. Two waiters, one table ==\n50 waiters tried to seat a party at the only table: seated=1"},"tests":{"file":"Tests.java","cases":["seating picks the smallest table that fits","table is freed when the party pays","order lifecycle only allows legal transitions","listeners are notified of every transition without the order knowing them","billing: price snapshot, cancelled excluded, discount then tax","discount strategies plug in; discount is capped at the subtotal","checkout and ordering guard rails","reservations reuse the table model","64 concurrent waiters, one table: one party seated","100 concurrent waiters, 10 tables: no table seated twice","100 concurrent orders on one visit: none lost, ids unique","concurrent advance of one order: exactly one transition wins"],"body":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\npublic class Tests {\n  static int passed = 0;\n\n  static void check(boolean cond, String msg) { if (!cond) throw new AssertionError(msg); }\n\n  static void expect(Class<? extends Throwable> type, Runnable r, String msg) {\n    try {\n      r.run();\n    } catch (Throwable t) {\n      if (type.isInstance(t)) return;\n      throw new AssertionError(msg + \" (threw \" + t + \")\");\n    }\n    throw new AssertionError(msg + \" (nothing thrown)\");\n  }\n\n  static void pass(String name) { passed++; System.out.println(\"PASS: \" + name); }\n\n  static Map<String, Integer> items(Object... pairs) {\n    Map<String, Integer> m = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < pairs.length; i += 2) m.put((String) pairs[i], (Integer) pairs[i + 1]);\n    return m;\n  }\n\n  static Menu menu() {\n    Menu m = new Menu();\n    m.add(\"Pasta\", 1200);\n    m.add(\"Cola\", 250);\n    m.add(\"Tiramisu\", 700);\n    return m;\n  }\n\n  static RestaurantService restaurant(TableService ts) { return new RestaurantService(ts, menu()); }\n\n  static void serve(Order o) {\n    o.advance(OrderStatus.PREPARING);\n    o.advance(OrderStatus.READY);\n    o.advance(OrderStatus.SERVED);\n  }\n\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    TableService ts = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 2), new Table(2, 2), new Table(3, 4), new Table(4, 6)));\n    RestaurantService r = restaurant(ts);\n    check(r.seatParty(2).table().id() == 1, \"party of 2 gets the first 2-seater\");\n    check(r.seatParty(2).table().id() == 2, \"next party of 2 gets the other 2-seater\");\n    check(r.seatParty(2).table().capacity() == 4, \"then falls back to the 4-seater\");\n    check(r.seatParty(5).table().capacity() == 6, \"party of 5 gets the 6-seater\");\n    expect(NoTableAvailableException.class, () -> r.seatParty(1), \"all tables taken\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> r.seatParty(0), \"zero party size\");\n    pass(\"seating picks the smallest table that fits\");\n\n    TableService t2 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 4)));\n    RestaurantService r2 = restaurant(t2);\n    Visit v = r2.seatParty(4);\n    check(t2.availableCount() == 0, \"table taken\");\n    serve(r2.placeOrder(v, items(\"Cola\", 1)));\n    r2.checkout(v, new NoDiscount());\n    check(t2.availableCount() == 1, \"paying frees the table\");\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> t2.free(v.table()), \"freeing a free table is an error\");\n    r2.seatParty(1);\n    pass(\"table is freed when the party pays\");\n\n    check(!OrderStatus.PLACED.canMoveTo(OrderStatus.READY), \"PLACED -> READY illegal\");\n    check(!OrderStatus.PLACED.canMoveTo(OrderStatus.SERVED), \"PLACED -> SERVED illegal\");\n    check(!OrderStatus.PREPARING.canMoveTo(OrderStatus.CANCELLED), \"cannot cancel once preparing\");\n    check(!OrderStatus.READY.canMoveTo(OrderStatus.PREPARING), \"no going backwards\");\n    check(!OrderStatus.SERVED.canMoveTo(OrderStatus.PREPARING), \"SERVED is terminal\");\n    check(!OrderStatus.CANCELLED.canMoveTo(OrderStatus.PLACED), \"CANCELLED is terminal\");\n    check(OrderStatus.PLACED.canMoveTo(OrderStatus.PREPARING) && OrderStatus.PLACED.canMoveTo(OrderStatus.CANCELLED), \"legal first moves\");\n    TableService t3 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 4)));\n    RestaurantService r3 = restaurant(t3);\n    Visit v3 = r3.seatParty(2);\n    Order o = r3.placeOrder(v3, items(\"Pasta\", 1));\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> o.advance(OrderStatus.READY), \"skipping PREPARING rejected\");\n    check(o.status() == OrderStatus.PLACED, \"failed move leaves status unchanged\");\n    serve(o);\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> o.advance(OrderStatus.CANCELLED), \"cannot cancel a served order\");\n    pass(\"order lifecycle only allows legal transitions\");\n\n    TableService t4 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 4)));\n    RestaurantService r4 = restaurant(t4);\n    List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n    r4.addListener((order, from, to) -> log.add(from + \">\" + to));\n    Visit v4 = r4.seatParty(2);\n    Order lo = r4.placeOrder(v4, items(\"Cola\", 2));\n    serve(lo);\n    check(log.equals(List.of(\"null>PLACED\", \"PLACED>PREPARING\", \"PREPARING>READY\", \"READY>SERVED\")), \"listener saw every step: \" + log);\n    List<String> late = new ArrayList<>();\n    r4.addListener((order, from, to) -> late.add(\"\" + to));\n    Order lo2 = r4.placeOrder(v4, items(\"Cola\", 1));\n    lo2.advance(OrderStatus.CANCELLED);\n    check(late.equals(List.of(\"PLACED\", \"CANCELLED\")), \"a listener added later gets events for new orders: \" + late);\n    pass(\"listeners are notified of every transition without the order knowing them\");\n\n    TableService t5 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 4)));\n    Menu m5 = menu();\n    RestaurantService r5 = new RestaurantService(t5, m5);\n    Visit v5 = r5.seatParty(2);\n    Order a = r5.placeOrder(v5, items(\"Pasta\", 2, \"Cola\", 3));        // 2400 + 750 = 3150\n    m5.reprice(\"Pasta\", 9999);\n    check(a.subtotalCents() == 3150, \"price snapshot survives a menu change: \" + a.subtotalCents());\n    Order b = r5.placeOrder(v5, items(\"Tiramisu\", 1));\n    serve(a);\n    b.advance(OrderStatus.CANCELLED);\n    Bill bill = r5.checkout(v5, new PercentOff(10));\n    check(bill.subtotalCents == 3150, \"cancelled order excluded: \" + bill.subtotalCents);\n    check(bill.discountCents == 315, \"10% of 3150\");\n    check(bill.taxCents == 141, \"5% of 2835 rounds down to 141: \" + bill.taxCents);\n    check(bill.totalCents == 2976, \"total is 2976: \" + bill.totalCents);\n    pass(\"billing: price snapshot, cancelled excluded, discount then tax\");\n\n    Order x1 = Order.create(1, new Table(9, 2), List.of(new OrderItem(new MenuItem(\"A\", 1000), 1)), List.of());\n    check(new BillingService().billFor(List.of(x1), new FlatOff(100000)).totalCents == 0, \"discount never exceeds subtotal\");\n    check(new BillingService().billFor(List.of(x1), new NoDiscount()).totalCents == 1050, \"no discount: 1000 + 5% tax\");\n    check(new BestOf(new PercentOff(10), new FlatOff(500)).discountFor(1000) == 500, \"BestOf picks the larger saving\");\n    check(new BestOf(new PercentOff(10), new FlatOff(500)).discountFor(10000) == 1000, \"BestOf picks 10% when it saves more\");\n    pass(\"discount strategies plug in; discount is capped at the subtotal\");\n\n    TableService t6 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 4)));\n    RestaurantService r6 = restaurant(t6);\n    Visit v6 = r6.seatParty(2);\n    Order p6 = r6.placeOrder(v6, items(\"Cola\", 1));\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> r6.checkout(v6, new NoDiscount()), \"cannot pay while an order is in progress\");\n    serve(p6);\n    r6.checkout(v6, new NoDiscount());\n    List<String> seen6 = new ArrayList<>();\n    r6.addListener((order, from, to) -> seen6.add(\"\" + to));\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> r6.placeOrder(v6, items(\"Cola\", 1)), \"cannot order on a closed visit\");\n    check(seen6.isEmpty(), \"a rejected order is never announced to the kitchen: \" + seen6);\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> r6.placeOrder(r6.seatParty(1), items(\"Sushi\", 1)), \"unknown menu item\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> new OrderItem(new MenuItem(\"A\", 1), 0), \"zero quantity\");\n    pass(\"checkout and ordering guard rails\");\n\n    TableService t7 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 2), new Table(2, 4)));\n    Table res = t7.reserve(3).orElseThrow();\n    check(res.id() == 2 && t7.availableCount() == 1, \"reserved table is no longer available\");\n    check(t7.seat(3).isEmpty(), \"reserved table cannot be given away\");\n    t7.seatReserved(res);\n    expect(IllegalStateException.class, () -> t7.seatReserved(res), \"cannot seat the same reservation twice\");\n    pass(\"reservations reuse the table model\");\n\n    TableService t8 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 2)));\n    AtomicInteger seated = new AtomicInteger();\n    runAll(16, 64, () -> { if (t8.seat(2).isPresent()) seated.incrementAndGet(); });\n    check(seated.get() == 1, \"exactly one party gets the only table, got \" + seated.get());\n    pass(\"64 concurrent waiters, one table: one party seated\");\n\n    List<Table> ten = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) ten.add(new Table(i, 4));\n    TableService t9 = new TableService(ten);\n    Set<Integer> given = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n    AtomicInteger dup = new AtomicInteger();\n    runAll(16, 100, () -> t9.seat(4).ifPresent(t -> { if (!given.add(t.id())) dup.incrementAndGet(); }));\n    check(given.size() == 10 && dup.get() == 0, \"10 distinct tables handed out, duplicates=\" + dup.get());\n    pass(\"100 concurrent waiters, 10 tables: no table seated twice\");\n\n    TableService t10 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 4)));\n    RestaurantService r10 = restaurant(t10);\n    Visit v10 = r10.seatParty(2);\n    Set<Long> ids = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n    runAll(16, 100, () -> ids.add(r10.placeOrder(v10, items(\"Cola\", 1)).id()));\n    check(ids.size() == 100 && v10.orders().size() == 100, \"100 orders on one visit, unique ids: \" + ids.size());\n    pass(\"100 concurrent orders on one visit: none lost, ids unique\");\n\n    TableService t11 = new TableService(List.of(new Table(1, 4)));\n    Order shared = restaurant(t11).placeOrder(restaurant(t11).seatParty(2), items(\"Cola\", 1));\n    AtomicInteger moved = new AtomicInteger();\n    runAll(8, 20, () -> {\n      try { shared.advance(OrderStatus.PREPARING); moved.incrementAndGet(); } catch (IllegalStateException ignored) { }\n    });\n    check(moved.get() == 1, \"only one thread advances PLACED -> PREPARING, got \" + moved.get());\n    pass(\"concurrent advance of one order: exactly one transition wins\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"All \" + passed + \" tests passed\");\n  }\n\n  static void runAll(int threads, int jobs, Runnable job) throws Exception {\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(threads);\n    CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    List<Future<?>> fs = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < jobs; i++) fs.add(pool.submit(() -> { go.await(); job.run(); return null; }));\n    go.countDown();\n    for (Future<?> f : fs) f.get();\n    pool.shutdown();\n  }\n}","output":"PASS: seating picks the smallest table that fits\nPASS: table is freed when the party pays\nPASS: order lifecycle only allows legal transitions\nPASS: listeners are notified of every transition without the order knowing them\nPASS: billing: price snapshot, cancelled excluded, discount then tax\nPASS: discount strategies plug in; discount is capped at the subtotal\nPASS: checkout and ordering guard rails\nPASS: reservations reuse the table model\nPASS: 64 concurrent waiters, one table: one party seated\nPASS: 100 concurrent waiters, 10 tables: no table seated twice\nPASS: 100 concurrent orders on one visit: none lost, ids unique\nPASS: concurrent advance of one order: exactly one transition wins\nAll 12 tests passed"},"complexity":["Seat a party: O(T) scan over T tables, under one lock.","Advance an order: O(1) plus the listeners.","Bill: O(O x I) over O orders with I items each.","Place an order: O(I) to price I lines."]});
window.SOLUTIONS.push({"id":"concert-ticket-booking","intro":"A seat is `AVAILABLE`, `HELD` or `SOLD`, and a hold is a time-limited claim whose own small state machine (`ACTIVE`, `PAYING`, `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED`) decides who may pay, confirm or release it. Payment is slow and can fail, so it runs outside every lock, and the hold is re-checked afterwards. Every file compiles with plain `javac`; the demo output and test results below are from a real run, including the concurrency scenarios.","steps":[{"title":"Requirement 1: events, sections and the seat lifecycle","text":"Each transition on `EventSeat` is a `synchronized` method that checks the current state first. `tryHold` succeeds on an available seat or one whose hold has lapsed; `confirm` works only for the holder before expiry; `release` works only for the holder and never touches a sold seat. A lapsed hold counts as free even before anything sweeps it. `Event` builds numbered sections and general-admission sections, and `describe` is what a customer sees when they list events.","code":[{"file":"SeatStatus.java","body":"public enum SeatStatus { AVAILABLE, HELD, SOLD }"},{"file":"Section.java","body":"public class Section {\n  private final String name;\n  private final Money price;\n\n  public Section(String name, Money price) {\n    this.name = name;\n    this.price = price;\n  }\n\n  public String getName() { return name; }\n  public Money getPrice() { return price; }\n}"},{"file":"EventSeat.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\n\npublic class EventSeat {\n  private final String id;\n  private final Section section;\n  private SeatStatus status = SeatStatus.AVAILABLE;\n  private String heldBy;\n  private Instant holdExpiresAt;\n\n  public EventSeat(String id, Section section) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.section = section;\n  }\n\n  // Available (or expired hold) -> Held. Returns false if someone else has it.\n  synchronized boolean tryHold(String userId, Instant now, Instant expiresAt) {\n    boolean expired = status == SeatStatus.HELD && !now.isBefore(holdExpiresAt);\n    if (status == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE || expired) {\n      status = SeatStatus.HELD;\n      heldBy = userId;\n      holdExpiresAt = expiresAt;\n      return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // Held by this user and not expired -> Sold.\n  synchronized boolean confirm(String userId, Instant now) {\n    if (status == SeatStatus.HELD && userId.equals(heldBy) && now.isBefore(holdExpiresAt)) {\n      status = SeatStatus.SOLD;\n      return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // Only the holder can release, and a sold seat never goes back on sale.\n  synchronized void release(String userId) {\n    if (status == SeatStatus.HELD && userId.equals(heldBy)) {\n      status = SeatStatus.AVAILABLE;\n      heldBy = null;\n      holdExpiresAt = null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // A lapsed hold counts as free even before anyone sweeps it.\n  public synchronized boolean isAvailable(Instant now) {\n    return status == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE || (status == SeatStatus.HELD && !now.isBefore(holdExpiresAt));\n  }\n\n  public String getId() { return id; }\n  public Section getSection() { return section; }\n  public synchronized SeatStatus getStatus() { return status; }\n  public synchronized String getHeldBy() { return heldBy; }\n}"},{"file":"Event.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Event {\n  private final String id;\n  private final String name;\n  private final List<Section> sections = new ArrayList<>();\n  private final Map<String, EventSeat> seats = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n  private final Map<String, GeneralAdmissionPool> pools = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n\n  public Event(String id, String name) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.name = name;\n  }\n\n  // Numbered seats: prefix + 1..count, e.g. V1, V2, ...\n  public void addSeats(Section section, String prefix, int count) {\n    sections.add(section);\n    for (int i = 1; i <= count; i++) {\n      EventSeat s = new EventSeat(prefix + i, section);\n      seats.put(s.getId(), s);\n    }\n  }\n\n  public void addGeneralAdmission(Section section, int capacity) {\n    sections.add(section);\n    pools.put(section.getName(), new GeneralAdmissionPool(section, capacity));\n  }\n\n  public EventSeat seat(String id) {\n    EventSeat s = seats.get(id);\n    if (s == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Unknown seat \" + id);\n    return s;\n  }\n\n  public GeneralAdmissionPool pool(String sectionName) {\n    GeneralAdmissionPool p = pools.get(sectionName);\n    if (p == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(sectionName + \" is not a general-admission section\");\n    return p;\n  }\n\n  public List<String> describe(Instant now) {\n    List<String> lines = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (Section s : sections) {\n      GeneralAdmissionPool pool = pools.get(s.getName());\n      String avail;\n      if (pool != null) {\n        avail = pool.remaining() + \" tickets left (general admission)\";\n      } else {\n        long total = seats.values().stream().filter(x -> x.getSection() == s).count();\n        long free = seats.values().stream().filter(x -> x.getSection() == s && x.isAvailable(now)).count();\n        avail = free + \"/\" + total + \" seats free\";\n      }\n      lines.add(String.format(\"%-8s %8s  %s\", s.getName(), s.getPrice(), avail));\n    }\n    return lines;\n  }\n\n  public String getId() { return id; }\n  public String getName() { return name; }\n}"},{"file":"EventCatalog.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class EventCatalog {\n  private final List<Event> events = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public void add(Event e) { events.add(e); }\n  public List<Event> list() { return new ArrayList<>(events); }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 2: holding up to six seats for ten minutes","text":"A hold claims every requested seat or none. The request is validated first (one to six seats, no duplicates), every seat id is resolved before any seat is touched (so an unknown id leaves nothing held), and seats are claimed in sorted order. Sorting gives every request the same global order, so two users asking for the same pair in opposite order cannot deadlock or both fail: whoever gets the first seat also gets the second. If any seat is taken, the ones already claimed are released.","code":[{"file":"HoldService.java  ›  hold","body":"public Hold hold(Event event, String userId, List<String> seatIds) {\n  if (seatIds.isEmpty() || seatIds.size() > MAX_TICKETS)\n    throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Choose 1 to \" + MAX_TICKETS + \" seats\");\n  TreeSet<String> ordered = new TreeSet<>(seatIds);        // one global order for every request\n  if (ordered.size() != seatIds.size()) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Duplicate seat in request\");\n\n  List<EventSeat> wanted = new ArrayList<>();\n  for (String id : ordered) wanted.add(event.seat(id));    // unknown ids fail before anything is held\n\n  Instant now = clock.instant();\n  Instant expiry = now.plus(HOLD_FOR);\n  List<EventSeat> taken = new ArrayList<>();\n  for (EventSeat seat : wanted) {\n    if (!seat.tryHold(userId, now, expiry)) {\n      taken.forEach(s -> s.release(userId));               // all or nothing\n      throw new SeatUnavailableException(\"Seat \" + seat.getId());\n    }\n    taken.add(seat);\n  }\n  Hold hold = new Hold(ids.incrementAndGet(), userId, taken, null, 0, expiry);\n  holds.put(hold.getId(), hold);\n  return hold;\n}"},{"file":"SeatUnavailableException.java","body":"public class SeatUnavailableException extends RuntimeException {\n  public SeatUnavailableException(String what) { super(what + \" is not available\"); }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirement 5: general admission by capacity","text":"A general-admission section has no seat ids, just a count. `GeneralAdmissionPool` is a counter guarded by a lock, and the same `Hold` carries the ticket quantity, so these sales go through the same confirm, release and expiry path as numbered seats.","code":[{"file":"GeneralAdmissionPool.java","body":"public class GeneralAdmissionPool {\n  private final Section section;\n  private int remaining;\n\n  public GeneralAdmissionPool(Section section, int capacity) {\n    this.section = section;\n    this.remaining = capacity;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized boolean tryReserve(int qty) {\n    if (qty <= 0 || qty > remaining) return false;\n    remaining -= qty;\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized void giveBack(int qty) { remaining += qty; }\n  public synchronized int remaining() { return remaining; }\n  public Section getSection() { return section; }\n}"},{"file":"HoldService.java  ›  holdGeneralAdmission","body":"public Hold holdGeneralAdmission(Event event, String userId, String sectionName, int quantity) {\n  if (quantity < 1 || quantity > MAX_TICKETS)\n    throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Choose 1 to \" + MAX_TICKETS + \" tickets\");\n  GeneralAdmissionPool pool = event.pool(sectionName);\n  if (!pool.tryReserve(quantity)) throw new SeatUnavailableException(sectionName + \" (\" + quantity + \" ticket(s))\");\n  Hold hold = new Hold(ids.incrementAndGet(), userId, List.of(), pool, quantity, clock.instant().plus(HOLD_FOR));\n  holds.put(hold.getId(), hold);\n  return hold;\n}"}]},{"title":"The hold's own state machine","text":"`beginPayment` lets exactly one caller start paying, and only while the hold is live, which stops a double click from charging twice. `confirm` is valid only for the payer and only before expiry. `expireIfDue` is used by the sweeper and ignores holds being paid for, so the sweeper can never race with an in-flight payment.","code":[{"file":"Hold.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// A time-limited claim. Its state machine decides who may pay, confirm or release it.\npublic class Hold {\n  public enum State { ACTIVE, PAYING, CONFIRMED, RELEASED }\n\n  private final long id;\n  private final String userId;\n  private final List<EventSeat> seats;\n  private final GeneralAdmissionPool pool;     // null for numbered seats\n  private final int gaQuantity;\n  private final Instant expiresAt;\n  private State state = State.ACTIVE;\n\n  public Hold(long id, String userId, List<EventSeat> seats, GeneralAdmissionPool pool, int gaQuantity, Instant expiresAt) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.userId = userId;\n    this.seats = seats;\n    this.pool = pool;\n    this.gaQuantity = gaQuantity;\n    this.expiresAt = expiresAt;\n  }\n\n  // Exactly one caller can start paying, and only while the hold is live.\n  synchronized boolean beginPayment(Instant now) {\n    if (state == State.ACTIVE && now.isBefore(expiresAt)) { state = State.PAYING; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // Payment succeeded: only valid if we are still the payer and the hold has not lapsed.\n  synchronized boolean confirm(Instant now) {\n    if (state == State.PAYING && now.isBefore(expiresAt)) { state = State.CONFIRMED; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  synchronized boolean cancel() {\n    if (state == State.ACTIVE || state == State.PAYING) { state = State.RELEASED; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // The sweeper only touches holds nobody is paying for.\n  synchronized boolean expireIfDue(Instant now) {\n    if (state == State.ACTIVE && !now.isBefore(expiresAt)) { state = State.RELEASED; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  public Money total() {\n    Money sum = seats.stream().map(s -> s.getSection().getPrice()).reduce(Money.ZERO, Money::plus);\n    if (pool != null) sum = sum.plus(pool.getSection().getPrice().times(gaQuantity));\n    return sum;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized State getState() { return state; }\n  public long getId() { return id; }\n  public String getUserId() { return userId; }\n  public List<EventSeat> getSeats() { return seats; }\n  public GeneralAdmissionPool getPool() { return pool; }\n  public int getGaQuantity() { return gaQuantity; }\n  public Instant getExpiresAt() { return expiresAt; }\n}"}]},{"title":"Requirements 3 and 4: pay, confirm, or release","text":"The order of operations is the important part. First claim the right to pay: an expired or already-used hold fails here, before any money moves. Then charge, outside every lock. If the payment fails, release the seats at once. If it succeeds, confirm the hold: when the hold lapsed while we were paying, refund and release, because the seat may now belong to someone else. Only after a successful confirm are the seats marked sold.","code":[{"file":"BookingService.java  ›  confirm","body":"public Booking confirm(long holdId, PaymentMethod method) {\n  Hold hold = holds.get(holdId);\n\n  // Claim the right to pay. A double click, or a hold that already lapsed, fails here, before any money moves.\n  if (!hold.beginPayment(clock.instant())) throw new HoldExpiredException(holdId);\n\n  PaymentResult paid;\n  try {\n    paid = method.charge(hold.getUserId(), hold.total());   // slow, so it runs outside every lock\n  } catch (PaymentFailedException e) {\n    holds.release(hold);                                    // seats go back on sale at once\n    throw e;\n  }\n\n  Instant now = clock.instant();\n  if (!hold.confirm(now)) {                                 // the hold lapsed while we were paying\n    method.refund(paid);\n    holds.release(hold);\n    throw new HoldExpiredException(holdId);\n  }\n  for (EventSeat seat : hold.getSeats()) {\n    if (!seat.confirm(hold.getUserId(), now))\n      throw new IllegalStateException(\"Seat \" + seat.getId() + \" lost despite a confirmed hold\");\n  }\n  holds.forget(hold);\n\n  Booking booking = new Booking(eventName, hold.getUserId(), hold.getSeats(), hold.getGaQuantity(), hold.total(), paid.reference());\n  for (BookingListener l : listeners) {\n    try {\n      l.onBooked(booking);\n    } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n      System.err.println(\"Listener failed: \" + e);          // a broken listener must not undo a sale\n    }\n  }\n  return booking;\n}"},{"file":"HoldService.java  ›  release","body":"// Used when payment fails or the user walks away. A confirmed hold cannot be released.\npublic void release(Hold hold) {\n  if (hold.cancel()) giveBack(hold);\n}"},{"file":"HoldService.java  ›  releaseExpired","body":"// Run on a schedule (e.g. every few seconds) to return lapsed holds, GA capacity included.\npublic int releaseExpired() {\n  Instant now = clock.instant();\n  int released = 0;\n  for (Hold h : holds.values()) {\n    if (h.expireIfDue(now)) { giveBack(h); released++; }\n  }\n  return released;\n}"},{"file":"HoldExpiredException.java","body":"public class HoldExpiredException extends RuntimeException {\n  public HoldExpiredException(long holdId) { super(\"Hold \" + holdId + \" has expired or was already used\"); }\n}"}]},{"title":"Extensibility: payment methods and booking events","text":"`PaymentMethod` is a strategy, so a new method is a new class and the booking flow never changes. `BookingService` publishes a `BookingListener` event after a sale; email and analytics are two listeners, and one that throws cannot undo the sale.","code":[{"file":"PaymentResult.java","body":"public record PaymentResult(String reference, Money amount) { }"},{"file":"PaymentMethod.java","body":"public interface PaymentMethod {\n  PaymentResult charge(String userId, Money amount);\n  void refund(PaymentResult result);\n}"},{"file":"CardPayment.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\n// Stand-in for a card gateway: numbers ending in 0000 are declined.\npublic class CardPayment implements PaymentMethod {\n  private static final AtomicLong counter = new AtomicLong();\n\n  private final String cardNumber;\n  private final List<String> refunds = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public CardPayment(String cardNumber) { this.cardNumber = cardNumber; }\n\n  public PaymentResult charge(String userId, Money amount) {\n    if (cardNumber.endsWith(\"0000\")) throw new PaymentFailedException(\"Card declined\");\n    return new PaymentResult(\"CARD-\" + counter.incrementAndGet(), amount);\n  }\n\n  public void refund(PaymentResult result) { refunds.add(result.reference()); }\n  public List<String> refunds() { return refunds; }\n}"},{"file":"UpiPayment.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\n// Stand-in for a UPI collect request: ids containing \"fail\" are rejected.\npublic class UpiPayment implements PaymentMethod {\n  private static final AtomicLong counter = new AtomicLong();\n\n  private final String vpa;\n  private final List<String> refunds = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public UpiPayment(String vpa) { this.vpa = vpa; }\n\n  public PaymentResult charge(String userId, Money amount) {\n    if (vpa.contains(\"fail\")) throw new PaymentFailedException(\"UPI request rejected\");\n    return new PaymentResult(\"UPI-\" + counter.incrementAndGet(), amount);\n  }\n\n  public void refund(PaymentResult result) { refunds.add(result.reference()); }\n  public List<String> refunds() { return refunds; }\n}"},{"file":"PaymentFailedException.java","body":"public class PaymentFailedException extends RuntimeException {\n  public PaymentFailedException(String reason) { super(reason); }\n}"},{"file":"Booking.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class Booking {\n  private final String eventName;\n  private final String userId;\n  private final List<String> seatIds;\n  private final int generalAdmissionTickets;\n  private final Money total;\n  private final String paymentReference;\n\n  public Booking(String eventName, String userId, List<EventSeat> seats, int gaTickets, Money total, String paymentReference) {\n    this.eventName = eventName;\n    this.userId = userId;\n    this.seatIds = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (EventSeat s : seats) seatIds.add(s.getId());\n    this.generalAdmissionTickets = gaTickets;\n    this.total = total;\n    this.paymentReference = paymentReference;\n  }\n\n  public int ticketCount() { return seatIds.size() + generalAdmissionTickets; }\n  public String getEventName() { return eventName; }\n  public String getUserId() { return userId; }\n  public List<String> getSeatIds() { return seatIds; }\n  public Money getTotal() { return total; }\n  public String getPaymentReference() { return paymentReference; }\n}"},{"file":"BookingListener.java","body":"public interface BookingListener {\n  void onBooked(Booking booking);\n}"},{"file":"ConfirmationEmailListener.java","body":"public class ConfirmationEmailListener implements BookingListener {\n  public void onBooked(Booking b) {\n    System.out.println(\"  [EMAIL] to \" + b.getUserId() + \": \" + b.ticketCount() + \" ticket(s) for \"\n        + b.getEventName() + \" confirmed, \" + b.getTotal() + \" (\" + b.getPaymentReference() + \")\");\n  }\n}"},{"file":"AnalyticsListener.java","body":"import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\npublic class AnalyticsListener implements BookingListener {\n  private final AtomicLong bookings = new AtomicLong();\n  private final AtomicLong tickets = new AtomicLong();\n  private final AtomicLong revenueCents = new AtomicLong();\n\n  public void onBooked(Booking b) {\n    bookings.incrementAndGet();\n    tickets.addAndGet(b.ticketCount());\n    revenueCents.addAndGet(b.getTotal().cents());\n  }\n\n  public String summary() {\n    return bookings + \" bookings, \" + tickets + \" tickets, \" + Money.ofCents(revenueCents.get());\n  }\n\n  public long bookings() { return bookings.get(); }\n}"}]}],"files":[{"file":"Money.java","body":"public final class Money {\n  public static final Money ZERO = new Money(0);\n\n  private final long cents;\n\n  private Money(long cents) { this.cents = cents; }\n\n  public static Money ofCents(long cents) { return new Money(cents); }\n  public static Money dollars(long dollars) { return new Money(dollars * 100); }\n\n  public Money plus(Money other) { return new Money(cents + other.cents); }\n  public Money times(long n) { return new Money(cents * n); }\n  public long cents() { return cents; }\n\n  @Override public boolean equals(Object o) { return o instanceof Money m && m.cents == cents; }\n  @Override public int hashCode() { return Long.hashCode(cents); }\n  @Override public String toString() { return String.format(\"$%d.%02d\", cents / 100, cents % 100); }\n}"},{"file":"MutableClock.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.time.ZoneId;\nimport java.time.ZoneOffset;\n\n// A clock we can move forward, so hold expiry can be shown and tested without waiting.\npublic class MutableClock extends Clock {\n  private Instant now;\n\n  public MutableClock(Instant start) { this.now = start; }\n\n  public synchronized void advance(Duration d) { now = now.plus(d); }\n\n  @Override public ZoneId getZone() { return ZoneOffset.UTC; }\n  @Override public Clock withZone(ZoneId zone) { return this; }\n  @Override public synchronized Instant instant() { return now; }\n}"},{"file":"SeatUnavailableException.java","body":"public class SeatUnavailableException extends RuntimeException {\n  public SeatUnavailableException(String what) { super(what + \" is not available\"); }\n}"},{"file":"HoldExpiredException.java","body":"public class HoldExpiredException extends RuntimeException {\n  public HoldExpiredException(long holdId) { super(\"Hold \" + holdId + \" has expired or was already used\"); }\n}"},{"file":"PaymentFailedException.java","body":"public class PaymentFailedException extends RuntimeException {\n  public PaymentFailedException(String reason) { super(reason); }\n}"},{"file":"SeatStatus.java","body":"public enum SeatStatus { AVAILABLE, HELD, SOLD }"},{"file":"Section.java","body":"public class Section {\n  private final String name;\n  private final Money price;\n\n  public Section(String name, Money price) {\n    this.name = name;\n    this.price = price;\n  }\n\n  public String getName() { return name; }\n  public Money getPrice() { return price; }\n}"},{"file":"EventSeat.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\n\npublic class EventSeat {\n  private final String id;\n  private final Section section;\n  private SeatStatus status = SeatStatus.AVAILABLE;\n  private String heldBy;\n  private Instant holdExpiresAt;\n\n  public EventSeat(String id, Section section) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.section = section;\n  }\n\n  // Available (or expired hold) -> Held. Returns false if someone else has it.\n  synchronized boolean tryHold(String userId, Instant now, Instant expiresAt) {\n    boolean expired = status == SeatStatus.HELD && !now.isBefore(holdExpiresAt);\n    if (status == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE || expired) {\n      status = SeatStatus.HELD;\n      heldBy = userId;\n      holdExpiresAt = expiresAt;\n      return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // Held by this user and not expired -> Sold.\n  synchronized boolean confirm(String userId, Instant now) {\n    if (status == SeatStatus.HELD && userId.equals(heldBy) && now.isBefore(holdExpiresAt)) {\n      status = SeatStatus.SOLD;\n      return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // Only the holder can release, and a sold seat never goes back on sale.\n  synchronized void release(String userId) {\n    if (status == SeatStatus.HELD && userId.equals(heldBy)) {\n      status = SeatStatus.AVAILABLE;\n      heldBy = null;\n      holdExpiresAt = null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // A lapsed hold counts as free even before anyone sweeps it.\n  public synchronized boolean isAvailable(Instant now) {\n    return status == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE || (status == SeatStatus.HELD && !now.isBefore(holdExpiresAt));\n  }\n\n  public String getId() { return id; }\n  public Section getSection() { return section; }\n  public synchronized SeatStatus getStatus() { return status; }\n  public synchronized String getHeldBy() { return heldBy; }\n}"},{"file":"GeneralAdmissionPool.java","body":"public class GeneralAdmissionPool {\n  private final Section section;\n  private int remaining;\n\n  public GeneralAdmissionPool(Section section, int capacity) {\n    this.section = section;\n    this.remaining = capacity;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized boolean tryReserve(int qty) {\n    if (qty <= 0 || qty > remaining) return false;\n    remaining -= qty;\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized void giveBack(int qty) { remaining += qty; }\n  public synchronized int remaining() { return remaining; }\n  public Section getSection() { return section; }\n}"},{"file":"Event.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Event {\n  private final String id;\n  private final String name;\n  private final List<Section> sections = new ArrayList<>();\n  private final Map<String, EventSeat> seats = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n  private final Map<String, GeneralAdmissionPool> pools = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n\n  public Event(String id, String name) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.name = name;\n  }\n\n  // Numbered seats: prefix + 1..count, e.g. V1, V2, ...\n  public void addSeats(Section section, String prefix, int count) {\n    sections.add(section);\n    for (int i = 1; i <= count; i++) {\n      EventSeat s = new EventSeat(prefix + i, section);\n      seats.put(s.getId(), s);\n    }\n  }\n\n  public void addGeneralAdmission(Section section, int capacity) {\n    sections.add(section);\n    pools.put(section.getName(), new GeneralAdmissionPool(section, capacity));\n  }\n\n  public EventSeat seat(String id) {\n    EventSeat s = seats.get(id);\n    if (s == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Unknown seat \" + id);\n    return s;\n  }\n\n  public GeneralAdmissionPool pool(String sectionName) {\n    GeneralAdmissionPool p = pools.get(sectionName);\n    if (p == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(sectionName + \" is not a general-admission section\");\n    return p;\n  }\n\n  public List<String> describe(Instant now) {\n    List<String> lines = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (Section s : sections) {\n      GeneralAdmissionPool pool = pools.get(s.getName());\n      String avail;\n      if (pool != null) {\n        avail = pool.remaining() + \" tickets left (general admission)\";\n      } else {\n        long total = seats.values().stream().filter(x -> x.getSection() == s).count();\n        long free = seats.values().stream().filter(x -> x.getSection() == s && x.isAvailable(now)).count();\n        avail = free + \"/\" + total + \" seats free\";\n      }\n      lines.add(String.format(\"%-8s %8s  %s\", s.getName(), s.getPrice(), avail));\n    }\n    return lines;\n  }\n\n  public String getId() { return id; }\n  public String getName() { return name; }\n}"},{"file":"EventCatalog.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class EventCatalog {\n  private final List<Event> events = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public void add(Event e) { events.add(e); }\n  public List<Event> list() { return new ArrayList<>(events); }\n}"},{"file":"Hold.java","body":"import java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// A time-limited claim. Its state machine decides who may pay, confirm or release it.\npublic class Hold {\n  public enum State { ACTIVE, PAYING, CONFIRMED, RELEASED }\n\n  private final long id;\n  private final String userId;\n  private final List<EventSeat> seats;\n  private final GeneralAdmissionPool pool;     // null for numbered seats\n  private final int gaQuantity;\n  private final Instant expiresAt;\n  private State state = State.ACTIVE;\n\n  public Hold(long id, String userId, List<EventSeat> seats, GeneralAdmissionPool pool, int gaQuantity, Instant expiresAt) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.userId = userId;\n    this.seats = seats;\n    this.pool = pool;\n    this.gaQuantity = gaQuantity;\n    this.expiresAt = expiresAt;\n  }\n\n  // Exactly one caller can start paying, and only while the hold is live.\n  synchronized boolean beginPayment(Instant now) {\n    if (state == State.ACTIVE && now.isBefore(expiresAt)) { state = State.PAYING; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // Payment succeeded: only valid if we are still the payer and the hold has not lapsed.\n  synchronized boolean confirm(Instant now) {\n    if (state == State.PAYING && now.isBefore(expiresAt)) { state = State.CONFIRMED; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  synchronized boolean cancel() {\n    if (state == State.ACTIVE || state == State.PAYING) { state = State.RELEASED; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // The sweeper only touches holds nobody is paying for.\n  synchronized boolean expireIfDue(Instant now) {\n    if (state == State.ACTIVE && !now.isBefore(expiresAt)) { state = State.RELEASED; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  public Money total() {\n    Money sum = seats.stream().map(s -> s.getSection().getPrice()).reduce(Money.ZERO, Money::plus);\n    if (pool != null) sum = sum.plus(pool.getSection().getPrice().times(gaQuantity));\n    return sum;\n  }\n\n  public synchronized State getState() { return state; }\n  public long getId() { return id; }\n  public String getUserId() { return userId; }\n  public List<EventSeat> getSeats() { return seats; }\n  public GeneralAdmissionPool getPool() { return pool; }\n  public int getGaQuantity() { return gaQuantity; }\n  public Instant getExpiresAt() { return expiresAt; }\n}"},{"file":"HoldService.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\npublic class HoldService {\n  static final int MAX_TICKETS = 6;\n  static final Duration HOLD_FOR = Duration.ofMinutes(10);\n\n  private final Clock clock;\n  private final AtomicLong ids = new AtomicLong();\n  private final Map<Long, Hold> holds = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n  public HoldService(Clock clock) { this.clock = clock; }\n\n  public Hold hold(Event event, String userId, List<String> seatIds) {\n    if (seatIds.isEmpty() || seatIds.size() > MAX_TICKETS)\n      throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Choose 1 to \" + MAX_TICKETS + \" seats\");\n    TreeSet<String> ordered = new TreeSet<>(seatIds);        // one global order for every request\n    if (ordered.size() != seatIds.size()) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Duplicate seat in request\");\n\n    List<EventSeat> wanted = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (String id : ordered) wanted.add(event.seat(id));    // unknown ids fail before anything is held\n\n    Instant now = clock.instant();\n    Instant expiry = now.plus(HOLD_FOR);\n    List<EventSeat> taken = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (EventSeat seat : wanted) {\n      if (!seat.tryHold(userId, now, expiry)) {\n        taken.forEach(s -> s.release(userId));               // all or nothing\n        throw new SeatUnavailableException(\"Seat \" + seat.getId());\n      }\n      taken.add(seat);\n    }\n    Hold hold = new Hold(ids.incrementAndGet(), userId, taken, null, 0, expiry);\n    holds.put(hold.getId(), hold);\n    return hold;\n  }\n\n  public Hold holdGeneralAdmission(Event event, String userId, String sectionName, int quantity) {\n    if (quantity < 1 || quantity > MAX_TICKETS)\n      throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Choose 1 to \" + MAX_TICKETS + \" tickets\");\n    GeneralAdmissionPool pool = event.pool(sectionName);\n    if (!pool.tryReserve(quantity)) throw new SeatUnavailableException(sectionName + \" (\" + quantity + \" ticket(s))\");\n    Hold hold = new Hold(ids.incrementAndGet(), userId, List.of(), pool, quantity, clock.instant().plus(HOLD_FOR));\n    holds.put(hold.getId(), hold);\n    return hold;\n  }\n\n  public Hold get(long holdId) {\n    Hold h = holds.get(holdId);\n    if (h == null) throw new HoldExpiredException(holdId);\n    return h;\n  }\n\n  // Used when payment fails or the user walks away. A confirmed hold cannot be released.\n  public void release(Hold hold) {\n    if (hold.cancel()) giveBack(hold);\n  }\n\n  // Run on a schedule (e.g. every few seconds) to return lapsed holds, GA capacity included.\n  public int releaseExpired() {\n    Instant now = clock.instant();\n    int released = 0;\n    for (Hold h : holds.values()) {\n      if (h.expireIfDue(now)) { giveBack(h); released++; }\n    }\n    return released;\n  }\n\n  void forget(Hold hold) { holds.remove(hold.getId()); }\n\n  private void giveBack(Hold hold) {\n    hold.getSeats().forEach(s -> s.release(hold.getUserId()));   // no-op if someone else now owns the seat\n    if (hold.getPool() != null) hold.getPool().giveBack(hold.getGaQuantity());\n    holds.remove(hold.getId());\n  }\n}"},{"file":"PaymentResult.java","body":"public record PaymentResult(String reference, Money amount) { }"},{"file":"PaymentMethod.java","body":"public interface PaymentMethod {\n  PaymentResult charge(String userId, Money amount);\n  void refund(PaymentResult result);\n}"},{"file":"CardPayment.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\n// Stand-in for a card gateway: numbers ending in 0000 are declined.\npublic class CardPayment implements PaymentMethod {\n  private static final AtomicLong counter = new AtomicLong();\n\n  private final String cardNumber;\n  private final List<String> refunds = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public CardPayment(String cardNumber) { this.cardNumber = cardNumber; }\n\n  public PaymentResult charge(String userId, Money amount) {\n    if (cardNumber.endsWith(\"0000\")) throw new PaymentFailedException(\"Card declined\");\n    return new PaymentResult(\"CARD-\" + counter.incrementAndGet(), amount);\n  }\n\n  public void refund(PaymentResult result) { refunds.add(result.reference()); }\n  public List<String> refunds() { return refunds; }\n}"},{"file":"UpiPayment.java","body":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\n// Stand-in for a UPI collect request: ids containing \"fail\" are rejected.\npublic class UpiPayment implements PaymentMethod {\n  private static final AtomicLong counter = new AtomicLong();\n\n  private final String vpa;\n  private final List<String> refunds = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public UpiPayment(String vpa) { this.vpa = vpa; }\n\n  public PaymentResult charge(String userId, Money amount) {\n    if (vpa.contains(\"fail\")) throw new PaymentFailedException(\"UPI request rejected\");\n    return new PaymentResult(\"UPI-\" + counter.incrementAndGet(), amount);\n  }\n\n  public void refund(PaymentResult result) { refunds.add(result.reference()); }\n  public List<String> refunds() { return refunds; }\n}"},{"file":"Booking.java","body":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class Booking {\n  private final String eventName;\n  private final String userId;\n  private final List<String> seatIds;\n  private final int generalAdmissionTickets;\n  private final Money total;\n  private final String paymentReference;\n\n  public Booking(String eventName, String userId, List<EventSeat> seats, int gaTickets, Money total, String paymentReference) {\n    this.eventName = eventName;\n    this.userId = userId;\n    this.seatIds = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (EventSeat s : seats) seatIds.add(s.getId());\n    this.generalAdmissionTickets = gaTickets;\n    this.total = total;\n    this.paymentReference = paymentReference;\n  }\n\n  public int ticketCount() { return seatIds.size() + generalAdmissionTickets; }\n  public String getEventName() { return eventName; }\n  public String getUserId() { return userId; }\n  public List<String> getSeatIds() { return seatIds; }\n  public Money getTotal() { return total; }\n  public String getPaymentReference() { return paymentReference; }\n}"},{"file":"BookingListener.java","body":"public interface BookingListener {\n  void onBooked(Booking booking);\n}"},{"file":"ConfirmationEmailListener.java","body":"public class ConfirmationEmailListener implements BookingListener {\n  public void onBooked(Booking b) {\n    System.out.println(\"  [EMAIL] to \" + b.getUserId() + \": \" + b.ticketCount() + \" ticket(s) for \"\n        + b.getEventName() + \" confirmed, \" + b.getTotal() + \" (\" + b.getPaymentReference() + \")\");\n  }\n}"},{"file":"AnalyticsListener.java","body":"import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\npublic class AnalyticsListener implements BookingListener {\n  private final AtomicLong bookings = new AtomicLong();\n  private final AtomicLong tickets = new AtomicLong();\n  private final AtomicLong revenueCents = new AtomicLong();\n\n  public void onBooked(Booking b) {\n    bookings.incrementAndGet();\n    tickets.addAndGet(b.ticketCount());\n    revenueCents.addAndGet(b.getTotal().cents());\n  }\n\n  public String summary() {\n    return bookings + \" bookings, \" + tickets + \" tickets, \" + Money.ofCents(revenueCents.get());\n  }\n\n  public long bookings() { return bookings.get(); }\n}"},{"file":"BookingService.java","body":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\npublic class BookingService {\n  private final HoldService holds;\n  private final Clock clock;\n  private final String eventName;\n  private final List<BookingListener> listeners = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n\n  public BookingService(HoldService holds, Clock clock, String eventName) {\n    this.holds = holds;\n    this.clock = clock;\n    this.eventName = eventName;\n  }\n\n  public void addListener(BookingListener l) { listeners.add(l); }\n\n  public Booking confirm(long holdId, PaymentMethod method) {\n    Hold hold = holds.get(holdId);\n\n    // Claim the right to pay. A double click, or a hold that already lapsed, fails here, before any money moves.\n    if (!hold.beginPayment(clock.instant())) throw new HoldExpiredException(holdId);\n\n    PaymentResult paid;\n    try {\n      paid = method.charge(hold.getUserId(), hold.total());   // slow, so it runs outside every lock\n    } catch (PaymentFailedException e) {\n      holds.release(hold);                                    // seats go back on sale at once\n      throw e;\n    }\n\n    Instant now = clock.instant();\n    if (!hold.confirm(now)) {                                 // the hold lapsed while we were paying\n      method.refund(paid);\n      holds.release(hold);\n      throw new HoldExpiredException(holdId);\n    }\n    for (EventSeat seat : hold.getSeats()) {\n      if (!seat.confirm(hold.getUserId(), now))\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"Seat \" + seat.getId() + \" lost despite a confirmed hold\");\n    }\n    holds.forget(hold);\n\n    Booking booking = new Booking(eventName, hold.getUserId(), hold.getSeats(), hold.getGaQuantity(), hold.total(), paid.reference());\n    for (BookingListener l : listeners) {\n      try {\n        l.onBooked(booking);\n      } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n        System.err.println(\"Listener failed: \" + e);          // a broken listener must not undo a sale\n      }\n    }\n    return booking;\n  }\n}"}],"driver":{"text":"The demo covers listing events, all-or-nothing holds, paying by card and UPI, a declined card releasing seats, a hold expiring, a payment that outlives its hold being refunded, general admission with the sweeper, and 200 fans racing for one seat and 50 tickets.","file":"Main.java","body":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    MutableClock clock = new MutableClock(Instant.parse(\"2026-06-01T10:00:00Z\"));\n    HoldService holds = new HoldService(clock);\n\n    Event show = new Event(\"e1\", \"Coldplay Live\");\n    show.addSeats(new Section(\"VIP\", Money.dollars(200)), \"V\", 4);\n    show.addSeats(new Section(\"Balcony\", Money.dollars(80)), \"B\", 6);\n    show.addGeneralAdmission(new Section(\"Floor\", Money.dollars(50)), 3);\n    EventCatalog catalog = new EventCatalog();\n    catalog.add(show);\n\n    BookingService booking = new BookingService(holds, clock, show.getName());\n    booking.addListener(new ConfirmationEmailListener());\n    AnalyticsListener analytics = new AnalyticsListener();\n    booking.addListener(analytics);\n\n    System.out.println(\"== 1. Events and prices ==\");\n    for (Event e : catalog.list()) {\n      System.out.println(e.getName());\n      e.describe(clock.instant()).forEach(l -> System.out.println(\"  \" + l));\n    }\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 2. Holding seats: all or nothing, max six ==\");\n    Hold alice = holds.hold(show, \"alice\", List.of(\"V1\", \"V2\"));\n    System.out.println(\"Alice holds V1, V2 for 10 minutes, total \" + alice.total());\n    attempt(\"Bob asks for V2 + V3\", () -> holds.hold(show, \"bob\", List.of(\"V2\", \"V3\")));\n    System.out.println(\"V3 is still free after Bob's failed request: \" + show.seat(\"V3\").getStatus());\n    attempt(\"Bob asks for 7 seats\", () -> holds.hold(show, \"bob\", List.of(\"B1\", \"B2\", \"B3\", \"B4\", \"B5\", \"B6\", \"V3\")));\n    attempt(\"Bob asks for seat Z9\", () -> holds.hold(show, \"bob\", List.of(\"B1\", \"Z9\")));\n    System.out.println(\"B1 untouched by the failed request: \" + show.seat(\"B1\").getStatus());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 3. Pay and confirm ==\");\n    Booking b1 = booking.confirm(alice.getId(), new CardPayment(\"4111111111111111\"));\n    System.out.println(\"Alice's booking: \" + b1.getSeatIds() + \" \" + b1.getTotal());\n    System.out.println(\"V1 is now \" + show.seat(\"V1\").getStatus());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 4. Payment fails: seats are released at once ==\");\n    Hold bob = holds.hold(show, \"bob\", List.of(\"V3\"));\n    attempt(\"Bob pays with a declined card\", () -> booking.confirm(bob.getId(), new CardPayment(\"4000000000000000\")));\n    System.out.println(\"V3 is \" + show.seat(\"V3\").getStatus() + \" again\");\n    Hold carol = holds.hold(show, \"carol\", List.of(\"V3\"));\n    Booking b2 = booking.confirm(carol.getId(), new UpiPayment(\"carol@bank\"));\n    System.out.println(\"Carol pays by UPI, same booking flow: \" + b2.getSeatIds());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 5. Hold expires ==\");\n    Hold dave = holds.hold(show, \"dave\", List.of(\"B1\"));\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofMinutes(10));\n    System.out.println(\"10 minutes later B1 reads as free: \" + show.seat(\"B1\").isAvailable(clock.instant()));\n    Hold erin = holds.hold(show, \"erin\", List.of(\"B1\"));\n    System.out.println(\"Erin takes B1, held by \" + show.seat(\"B1\").getHeldBy());\n    CardPayment davesCard = new CardPayment(\"4222222222222222\");\n    attempt(\"Dave tries to pay for his lapsed hold\", () -> booking.confirm(dave.getId(), davesCard));\n    System.out.println(\"Dave was charged nothing: refunds=\" + davesCard.refunds().size() + \", Erin still holds B1: \" + show.seat(\"B1\").getHeldBy());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 6. A late payment cannot resurrect an expired hold ==\");\n    Hold frank = holds.hold(show, \"frank\", List.of(\"B2\"));\n    PaymentMethod slow = new PaymentMethod() {\n      public PaymentResult charge(String userId, Money amount) {\n        System.out.println(\"  gateway: charging \" + amount + \" ... it takes 11 minutes\");\n        clock.advance(Duration.ofMinutes(11));\n        return new PaymentResult(\"SLOW-1\", amount);\n      }\n      public void refund(PaymentResult r) { System.out.println(\"  gateway: refunded \" + r.reference()); }\n    };\n    attempt(\"Frank's slow payment completes\", () -> booking.confirm(frank.getId(), slow));\n    System.out.println(\"B2 is \" + show.seat(\"B2\").getStatus() + \" (not sold)\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 7. General admission by capacity ==\");\n    Hold g1 = holds.holdGeneralAdmission(show, \"gus\", \"Floor\", 2);\n    Hold g2 = holds.holdGeneralAdmission(show, \"hana\", \"Floor\", 1);\n    System.out.println(\"Floor tickets left: \" + show.pool(\"Floor\").remaining());\n    attempt(\"Ivan asks for 1 Floor ticket\", () -> holds.holdGeneralAdmission(show, \"ivan\", \"Floor\", 1));\n    Booking gb = booking.confirm(g1.getId(), new CardPayment(\"4333333333333333\"));\n    System.out.println(\"Gus bought \" + gb.ticketCount() + \" Floor tickets for \" + gb.getTotal());\n    clock.advance(Duration.ofMinutes(10));\n    int swept = holds.releaseExpired();\n    System.out.println(\"Sweeper released \" + swept + \" lapsed holds (Dave's, Erin's and Hana's); Floor tickets left: \" + show.pool(\"Floor\").remaining());\n    Hold g3 = holds.holdGeneralAdmission(show, \"ivan\", \"Floor\", 1);\n    System.out.println(\"Ivan now gets one: hold \" + g3.getState());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 8. Many fans, one seat ==\");\n    Event big = new Event(\"e2\", \"Stadium Night\");\n    big.addSeats(new Section(\"Front\", Money.dollars(300)), \"F\", 1);\n    big.addGeneralAdmission(new Section(\"Lawn\", Money.dollars(40)), 50);\n    HoldService bigHolds = new HoldService(clock);\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(16);\n    CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    List<Future<int[]>> results = new java.util.ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < 200; i++) {\n      final String fan = \"fan\" + i;\n      results.add(pool.submit(() -> {\n        go.await();\n        int seat = 0, lawn = 0;\n        try { bigHolds.hold(big, fan, List.of(\"F1\")); seat = 1; } catch (SeatUnavailableException ignored) { }\n        try { bigHolds.holdGeneralAdmission(big, fan, \"Lawn\", 1); lawn = 1; } catch (SeatUnavailableException ignored) { }\n        return new int[] { seat, lawn };\n      }));\n    }\n    go.countDown();\n    int seatWinners = 0, lawnWinners = 0;\n    for (Future<int[]> f : results) { seatWinners += f.get()[0]; lawnWinners += f.get()[1]; }\n    pool.shutdown();\n    System.out.println(\"200 fans, 1 front seat -> holds granted: \" + seatWinners);\n    System.out.println(\"200 fans, 50 lawn tickets -> holds granted: \" + lawnWinners + \", left: \" + big.pool(\"Lawn\").remaining());\n\n    System.out.println(\"\\n== 9. Analytics listener ==\");\n    System.out.println(\"Bookings so far: \" + analytics.summary());\n  }\n\n  private static void attempt(String what, Runnable r) {\n    try {\n      r.run();\n      System.out.println(what + \" -> ok\");\n    } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n      System.out.println(what + \" -> \" + e.getClass().getSimpleName() + \": \" + e.getMessage());\n    }\n  }\n}","output":"== 1. Events and prices ==\nColdplay Live\n  VIP       $200.00  4/4 seats free\n  Balcony    $80.00  6/6 seats free\n  Floor      $50.00  3 tickets left (general admission)\n\n== 2. Holding seats: all or nothing, max six ==\nAlice holds V1, V2 for 10 minutes, total $400.00\nBob asks for V2 + V3 -> SeatUnavailableException: Seat V2 is not available\nV3 is still free after Bob's failed request: AVAILABLE\nBob asks for 7 seats -> IllegalArgumentException: Choose 1 to 6 seats\nBob asks for seat Z9 -> IllegalArgumentException: Unknown seat Z9\nB1 untouched by the failed request: AVAILABLE\n\n== 3. Pay and confirm ==\n  [EMAIL] to alice: 2 ticket(s) for Coldplay Live confirmed, $400.00 (CARD-1)\nAlice's booking: [V1, V2] $400.00\nV1 is now SOLD\n\n== 4. Payment fails: seats are released at once ==\nBob pays with a declined card -> PaymentFailedException: Card declined\nV3 is AVAILABLE again\n  [EMAIL] to carol: 1 ticket(s) for Coldplay Live confirmed, $200.00 (UPI-1)\nCarol pays by UPI, same booking flow: [V3]\n\n== 5. Hold expires ==\n10 minutes later B1 reads as free: true\nErin takes B1, held by erin\nDave tries to pay for his lapsed hold -> HoldExpiredException: Hold 4 has expired or was already used\nDave was charged nothing: refunds=0, Erin still holds B1: erin\n\n== 6. A late payment cannot resurrect an expired hold ==\n  gateway: charging $80.00 ... it takes 11 minutes\n  gateway: refunded SLOW-1\nFrank's slow payment completes -> HoldExpiredException: Hold 6 has expired or was already used\nB2 is AVAILABLE (not sold)\n\n== 7. General admission by capacity ==\nFloor tickets left: 0\nIvan asks for 1 Floor ticket -> SeatUnavailableException: Floor (1 ticket(s)) is not available\n  [EMAIL] to gus: 2 ticket(s) for Coldplay Live confirmed, $100.00 (CARD-2)\nGus bought 2 Floor tickets for $100.00\nSweeper released 3 lapsed holds (Dave's, Erin's and Hana's); Floor tickets left: 1\nIvan now gets one: hold ACTIVE\n\n== 8. Many fans, one seat ==\n200 fans, 1 front seat -> holds granted: 1\n200 fans, 50 lawn tickets -> holds granted: 50, left: 0\n\n== 9. Analytics listener ==\nBookings so far: 3 bookings, 5 tickets, $700.00"},"tests":{"file":"Tests.java","cases":["hold is all-or-nothing and leaves no partial holds behind","at most six tickets per hold; bad requests rejected","hold converts to a sale after payment and stays sold","payment failure releases the seats at once","expired hold fails before any money moves","a payment that outlives the hold is refunded, not honoured","cleaning up an expired hold never touches the seat's new owner","ten simultaneous pay clicks charge exactly once","64 concurrent holds on one seat: exactly one wins","opposite-order overlapping requests never deadlock and never both win (100 rounds)","150 concurrent GA requests against capacity 10: exactly 10 granted","sweeper returns lapsed seats and GA capacity, never sold ones","sweeper never races with an in-flight payment","booking events reach listeners; a failing listener cannot undo a sale","a new payment method needs no change to the booking flow","general-admission bookings sell by capacity","catalog lists sections, prices and live availability"],"body":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\npublic class Tests {\n  static int passed = 0;\n\n  static void check(boolean cond, String msg) { if (!cond) throw new AssertionError(msg); }\n\n  static void expect(Class<? extends Throwable> type, Runnable r, String msg) {\n    try {\n      r.run();\n    } catch (Throwable t) {\n      if (type.isInstance(t)) return;\n      throw new AssertionError(msg + \" (threw \" + t + \")\");\n    }\n    throw new AssertionError(msg + \" (nothing thrown)\");\n  }\n\n  static void pass(String name) { passed++; System.out.println(\"PASS: \" + name); }\n\n  static class Env {\n    MutableClock clock = new MutableClock(Instant.parse(\"2026-06-01T10:00:00Z\"));\n    HoldService holds = new HoldService(clock);\n    BookingService booking = new BookingService(holds, clock, \"Show\");\n    Event event = new Event(\"e\", \"Show\");\n\n    Env() {\n      event.addSeats(new Section(\"VIP\", Money.dollars(200)), \"V\", 8);\n      event.addGeneralAdmission(new Section(\"Floor\", Money.dollars(50)), 10);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Counts charges and refunds so tests can prove money only moved when it should.\n  static class CountingPayment implements PaymentMethod {\n    final AtomicInteger charges = new AtomicInteger(), refunds = new AtomicInteger();\n    Runnable duringCharge = () -> { };\n\n    public PaymentResult charge(String userId, Money amount) {\n      charges.incrementAndGet();\n      duringCharge.run();\n      return new PaymentResult(\"T-\" + charges.get(), amount);\n    }\n\n    public void refund(PaymentResult r) { refunds.incrementAndGet(); }\n  }\n\n  static void runAll(int threads, int jobs, Callable<?> job) throws Exception {\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(threads);\n    CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    List<Future<?>> fs = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (int i = 0; i < jobs; i++) fs.add(pool.submit(() -> { go.await(); return job.call(); }));\n    go.countDown();\n    for (Future<?> f : fs) f.get(10, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n    pool.shutdown();\n  }\n\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    Env e = new Env();\n    Hold h = e.holds.hold(e.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V2\", \"V1\"));\n    check(h.total().equals(Money.dollars(400)), \"two VIP seats cost $400\");\n    check(e.event.seat(\"V1\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.HELD, \"seat is held\");\n    check(h.getExpiresAt().equals(e.clock.instant().plus(Duration.ofMinutes(10))), \"hold lasts ten minutes\");\n    expect(SeatUnavailableException.class, () -> e.holds.hold(e.event, \"u2\", List.of(\"V3\", \"V1\")), \"overlapping request fails\");\n    check(e.event.seat(\"V3\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE, \"failed request rolled back: V3 untouched\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> e.holds.hold(e.event, \"u2\", List.of(\"V3\", \"NOPE\")), \"unknown seat\");\n    check(e.event.seat(\"V3\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE, \"unknown seat id held nothing\");\n    pass(\"hold is all-or-nothing and leaves no partial holds behind\");\n\n    Env lim = new Env();\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> lim.holds.hold(lim.event, \"u\", List.of()), \"empty request\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> lim.holds.hold(lim.event, \"u\", List.of(\"V1\", \"V2\", \"V3\", \"V4\", \"V5\", \"V6\", \"V7\")), \"seven seats\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> lim.holds.hold(lim.event, \"u\", List.of(\"V1\", \"V1\")), \"duplicate seat\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> lim.holds.holdGeneralAdmission(lim.event, \"u\", \"Floor\", 7), \"seven GA tickets\");\n    expect(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> lim.holds.holdGeneralAdmission(lim.event, \"u\", \"VIP\", 1), \"VIP is not GA\");\n    check(lim.holds.hold(lim.event, \"u\", List.of(\"V1\", \"V2\", \"V3\", \"V4\", \"V5\", \"V6\")).getSeats().size() == 6, \"exactly six is allowed\");\n    pass(\"at most six tickets per hold; bad requests rejected\");\n\n    Env pay = new Env();\n    CountingPayment card = new CountingPayment();\n    Hold ph = pay.holds.hold(pay.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\", \"V2\"));\n    Booking bk = pay.booking.confirm(ph.getId(), card);\n    check(bk.getSeatIds().equals(List.of(\"V1\", \"V2\")) && bk.getTotal().equals(Money.dollars(400)), \"booking contents\");\n    check(pay.event.seat(\"V1\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.SOLD, \"seat sold after payment\");\n    check(card.charges.get() == 1 && card.refunds.get() == 0, \"charged once, never refunded\");\n    pay.holds.release(ph);\n    check(pay.event.seat(\"V1\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.SOLD, \"releasing a confirmed hold cannot resell the seat\");\n    expect(SeatUnavailableException.class, () -> pay.holds.hold(pay.event, \"u2\", List.of(\"V1\")), \"sold seat cannot be held\");\n    expect(HoldExpiredException.class, () -> pay.booking.confirm(ph.getId(), card), \"confirmed hold cannot be paid twice\");\n    check(card.charges.get() == 1, \"no second charge\");\n    pass(\"hold converts to a sale after payment and stays sold\");\n\n    Env fail = new Env();\n    Hold fh = fail.holds.hold(fail.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\"));\n    expect(PaymentFailedException.class, () -> fail.booking.confirm(fh.getId(), new CardPayment(\"4000000000000000\")), \"declined card\");\n    check(fail.event.seat(\"V1\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE, \"failed payment releases seats immediately\");\n    check(fh.getState() == Hold.State.RELEASED, \"hold is released\");\n    fail.holds.hold(fail.event, \"u2\", List.of(\"V1\"));\n    pass(\"payment failure releases the seats at once\");\n\n    Env exp = new Env();\n    CountingPayment p1 = new CountingPayment();\n    Hold eh = exp.holds.hold(exp.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\"));\n    exp.clock.advance(Duration.ofMinutes(10));\n    check(exp.event.seat(\"V1\").isAvailable(exp.clock.instant()), \"lapsed hold reads as available\");\n    expect(HoldExpiredException.class, () -> exp.booking.confirm(eh.getId(), p1), \"expired hold cannot be paid\");\n    check(p1.charges.get() == 0, \"expired hold fails cheaply: no charge attempted\");\n    pass(\"expired hold fails before any money moves\");\n\n    Env late = new Env();\n    CountingPayment slow = new CountingPayment();\n    Hold lh = late.holds.hold(late.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\"));\n    slow.duringCharge = () -> late.clock.advance(Duration.ofMinutes(11));\n    expect(HoldExpiredException.class, () -> late.booking.confirm(lh.getId(), slow), \"late payment\");\n    check(slow.refunds.get() == 1, \"late payment is refunded\");\n    check(late.event.seat(\"V1\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE, \"seat not sold by a late payment\");\n    pass(\"a payment that outlives the hold is refunded, not honoured\");\n\n    Env steal = new Env();\n    CountingPayment slow2 = new CountingPayment();\n    Hold sh = steal.holds.hold(steal.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\"));\n    slow2.duringCharge = () -> {\n      steal.clock.advance(Duration.ofMinutes(11));\n      steal.holds.hold(steal.event, \"u2\", List.of(\"V1\"));       // another fan takes the lapsed seat\n    };\n    expect(HoldExpiredException.class, () -> steal.booking.confirm(sh.getId(), slow2), \"late payment after seat was re-held\");\n    check(\"u2\".equals(steal.event.seat(\"V1\").getHeldBy()), \"cleanup of the first hold must not release u2's seat\");\n    check(steal.event.seat(\"V1\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.HELD, \"u2 still holds V1\");\n    pass(\"cleaning up an expired hold never touches the seat's new owner\");\n\n    Env dbl = new Env();\n    CountingPayment once = new CountingPayment();\n    Hold dh = dbl.holds.hold(dbl.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\"));\n    AtomicInteger won = new AtomicInteger();\n    runAll(10, 10, () -> {\n      try { dbl.booking.confirm(dh.getId(), once); won.incrementAndGet(); } catch (HoldExpiredException ignored) { }\n      return null;\n    });\n    check(won.get() == 1 && once.charges.get() == 1, \"double-click pays once: bookings=\" + won + \" charges=\" + once.charges);\n    pass(\"ten simultaneous pay clicks charge exactly once\");\n\n    Env race = new Env();\n    AtomicInteger holdsGranted = new AtomicInteger();\n    runAll(16, 64, () -> {\n      try { race.holds.hold(race.event, \"u\" + Thread.currentThread().getName(), List.of(\"V1\")); holdsGranted.incrementAndGet(); }\n      catch (SeatUnavailableException ignored) { }\n      return null;\n    });\n    check(holdsGranted.get() == 1, \"one hold for one seat, got \" + holdsGranted.get());\n    pass(\"64 concurrent holds on one seat: exactly one wins\");\n\n    int bothWon = 0, noneWon = 0;\n    for (int round = 0; round < 100; round++) {\n      Env r = new Env();\n      AtomicInteger wins = new AtomicInteger();\n      CountDownLatch go = new CountDownLatch(1);\n      ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);\n      Future<?> a = pool.submit(() -> { go.await(); try { r.holds.hold(r.event, \"A\", List.of(\"V1\", \"V2\")); wins.incrementAndGet(); } catch (SeatUnavailableException ignored) { } return null; });\n      Future<?> b = pool.submit(() -> { go.await(); try { r.holds.hold(r.event, \"B\", List.of(\"V2\", \"V1\")); wins.incrementAndGet(); } catch (SeatUnavailableException ignored) { } return null; });\n      go.countDown();\n      a.get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n      b.get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n      pool.shutdown();\n      if (wins.get() == 2) bothWon++;\n      if (wins.get() == 0) noneWon++;\n    }\n    check(bothWon == 0, \"two users never both get overlapping seats\");\n    check(noneWon == 0, \"sorted lock order means one of two opposite-order requests always wins\");\n    pass(\"opposite-order overlapping requests never deadlock and never both win (100 rounds)\");\n\n    Env ga = new Env();\n    AtomicInteger gaWins = new AtomicInteger();\n    runAll(16, 150, () -> {\n      try {\n        ga.holds.holdGeneralAdmission(ga.event, \"g\", \"Floor\", 1);\n        gaWins.incrementAndGet();\n      } catch (SeatUnavailableException ignored) { }\n      return null;\n    });\n    check(gaWins.get() == 10 && ga.event.pool(\"Floor\").remaining() == 0, \"capacity of 10 sold exactly: \" + gaWins.get());\n    pass(\"150 concurrent GA requests against capacity 10: exactly 10 granted\");\n\n    Env sweep = new Env();\n    Hold g1 = sweep.holds.holdGeneralAdmission(sweep.event, \"u1\", \"Floor\", 4);\n    Hold g2 = sweep.holds.holdGeneralAdmission(sweep.event, \"u2\", \"Floor\", 3);\n    sweep.booking.confirm(g2.getId(), new CountingPayment());\n    Hold sv = sweep.holds.hold(sweep.event, \"u3\", List.of(\"V1\"));\n    check(sweep.event.pool(\"Floor\").remaining() == 3, \"7 of 10 reserved\");\n    sweep.clock.advance(Duration.ofMinutes(10));\n    check(sweep.holds.releaseExpired() == 2, \"sweeper releases the two unpaid holds (GA and seat)\");\n    check(sweep.event.pool(\"Floor\").remaining() == 7, \"only the unpaid 4 tickets returned; the 3 sold stay sold: \" + sweep.event.pool(\"Floor\").remaining());\n    check(sweep.event.seat(\"V1\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.AVAILABLE, \"seat released by sweeper\");\n    check(sweep.holds.releaseExpired() == 0, \"sweeper is idempotent\");\n    pass(\"sweeper returns lapsed seats and GA capacity, never sold ones\");\n\n    Env sw2 = new Env();\n    CountingPayment mid = new CountingPayment();\n    Hold payingHold = sw2.holds.hold(sw2.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\"));\n    mid.duringCharge = () -> { sw2.clock.advance(Duration.ofMinutes(11)); check(sw2.holds.releaseExpired() == 0, \"sweeper leaves a hold that is being paid for\"); };\n    expect(HoldExpiredException.class, () -> sw2.booking.confirm(payingHold.getId(), mid), \"paying hold that lapsed\");\n    check(mid.refunds.get() == 1, \"refund issued exactly once\");\n    pass(\"sweeper never races with an in-flight payment\");\n\n    Env ev = new Env();\n    CountingPayment c = new CountingPayment();\n    List<String> mails = new ArrayList<>();\n    AnalyticsListener analytics = new AnalyticsListener();\n    ev.booking.addListener(b -> mails.add(b.getUserId()));\n    ev.booking.addListener(analytics);\n    ev.booking.addListener(b -> { throw new IllegalStateException(\"analytics down\"); });\n    Booking made = ev.booking.confirm(ev.holds.hold(ev.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\", \"V2\")).getId(), c);\n    check(mails.equals(List.of(\"u1\")) && analytics.bookings() == 1, \"listeners received the booking\");\n    check(made.getTotal().equals(Money.dollars(400)) && ev.event.seat(\"V1\").getStatus() == SeatStatus.SOLD, \"a failing listener does not undo the sale\");\n    pass(\"booking events reach listeners; a failing listener cannot undo a sale\");\n\n    Env upi = new Env();\n    UpiPayment u = new UpiPayment(\"a@bank\");\n    check(upi.booking.confirm(upi.holds.hold(upi.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\")).getId(), u).getPaymentReference().startsWith(\"UPI-\"), \"UPI booking\");\n    expect(PaymentFailedException.class, () -> upi.booking.confirm(upi.holds.hold(upi.event, \"u2\", List.of(\"V2\")).getId(), new UpiPayment(\"fail@bank\")), \"UPI rejection\");\n    pass(\"a new payment method needs no change to the booking flow\");\n\n    Env gb = new Env();\n    Hold gh = gb.holds.holdGeneralAdmission(gb.event, \"u1\", \"Floor\", 3);\n    check(gh.total().equals(Money.dollars(150)), \"3 floor tickets at $50\");\n    Booking gbk = gb.booking.confirm(gh.getId(), new CountingPayment());\n    check(gbk.ticketCount() == 3 && gb.event.pool(\"Floor\").remaining() == 7, \"GA booking sells by capacity\");\n    pass(\"general-admission bookings sell by capacity\");\n\n    Env cat = new Env();\n    EventCatalog ec = new EventCatalog();\n    ec.add(cat.event);\n    cat.holds.hold(cat.event, \"u1\", List.of(\"V1\", \"V2\"));\n    List<String> lines = ec.list().get(0).describe(cat.clock.instant());\n    check(lines.get(0).contains(\"$200.00\") && lines.get(0).contains(\"6/8 seats free\"), \"VIP line: \" + lines.get(0));\n    check(lines.get(1).contains(\"10 tickets left\"), \"Floor line: \" + lines.get(1));\n    pass(\"catalog lists sections, prices and live availability\");\n\n    System.out.println(\"All \" + passed + \" tests passed\");\n  }\n}","output":"PASS: hold is all-or-nothing and leaves no partial holds behind\nPASS: at most six tickets per hold; bad requests rejected\nPASS: hold converts to a sale after payment and stays sold\nPASS: payment failure releases the seats at once\nPASS: expired hold fails before any money moves\nPASS: a payment that outlives the hold is refunded, not honoured\nPASS: cleaning up an expired hold never touches the seat's new owner\nPASS: ten simultaneous pay clicks charge exactly once\nPASS: 64 concurrent holds on one seat: exactly one wins\nPASS: opposite-order overlapping requests never deadlock and never both win (100 rounds)\nPASS: 150 concurrent GA requests against capacity 10: exactly 10 granted\nPASS: sweeper returns lapsed seats and GA capacity, never sold ones\nPASS: sweeper never races with an in-flight payment\nPASS: booking events reach listeners; a failing listener cannot undo a sale\nPASS: a new payment method needs no change to the booking flow\nPASS: general-admission bookings sell by capacity\nPASS: catalog lists sections, prices and live availability\nAll 17 tests passed"},"complexity":["Hold k seats (k at most 6): O(k log k) to sort, then O(k) to claim.","General-admission hold: O(1).","Confirm: O(k) after the payment call.","Sweeper: O(H) over the H live holds."]});
